2820
01:25:24,582 --> 01:25:25,983
<b>if I'd be willing to come work together.</b>

2821
01:25:26,017 --> 01:25:27,018
<b>And you rejected him again.</b>

2822
01:25:27,418 --> 01:25:28,386
<b>Uh, right.</b>

2823
01:25:28,386 --> 01:25:29,454
<b>Why this time?</b>

2824
01:25:30,188 --> 01:25:33,591
<b>This time because I had just started at NYU.</b>

2825
01:25:33,591 --> 01:25:34,459
<b>and</b>

2826
01:25:35,193 --> 01:25:36,627
<b>Mm. I think there were several reasons.</b>

2827
01:25:36,627 --> 01:25:37,995
<b>When I talked with him,</b>

2828
01:25:38,396 --> 01:25:39,230
<b>Uh,</b>

2829
01:25:39,363 --> 01:25:40,832
<b>the main topic we discussed</b>

2830
01:25:40,832 --> 01:25:42,033
<b>wasn't salary or anything like that.</b>

2831
01:25:42,033 --> 01:25:43,167
<b>We didn't talk about any of that.</b>

2832
01:25:43,267 --> 01:25:44,769
<b>The main topic was</b>

2833
01:25:44,802 --> 01:25:47,171
<b>how to give future artificial intelligence</b>

2834
01:25:47,271 --> 01:25:48,573
<b>the ability to love.</b>

2835
01:25:49,040 --> 01:25:50,808
<b>the ability to love.</b>

2836
01:25:50,808 --> 01:25:52,577
<b>Discussing philosophy.</b>

2837
01:25:52,577 --> 01:25:53,678
<b>Of course, I finally asked him</b>

2838
01:25:53,678 --> 01:25:54,078
<b>one question.</b>

2839
01:25:54,078 --> 01:25:57,648
<b>I asked how he viewed multimodality,</b>

2840
01:25:57,915 --> 01:26:00,218
<b>how he viewed computer vision,</b>

2841
01:26:00,218 --> 01:26:04,155
<b>or general perception models —</b>

2842
01:26:04,755 --> 01:26:06,224
<b>what did he think?</b>

2843
01:26:06,224 --> 01:26:07,725
<b>Ilya's response was</b>

2844
01:26:07,859 --> 01:26:10,661
<b>he felt this was already solved well enough.</b>

2845
01:26:11,129 --> 01:26:12,830
<b>Okay, so I thought</b>

2846
01:26:13,064 --> 01:26:14,265
<b>maybe, uh,</b>

2847
01:26:14,265 --> 01:26:17,568
<b>SSI has its own language-based</b>

2848
01:26:17,568 --> 01:26:19,337
<b>approach.</b>

2849
01:26:19,337 --> 01:26:20,471
<b>And that approach,</b>

2850
01:26:20,538 --> 01:26:21,873
<b>at least for now,</b>

2851
01:26:22,006 --> 01:26:24,208
<b>is not the path I want to pursue.</b>

2852
01:26:24,375 --> 01:26:26,177
<b>This is your fundamental disagreement —</b>

2853
01:26:26,277 --> 01:26:29,547
<b>LLM versus vision.</b>

2854
01:26:29,580 --> 01:26:31,449
<b>Right. We can talk more about this later.</b>

2855
01:26:31,449 --> 01:26:34,919
<b>But I don't actually see this as a disagreement.</b>

2856
01:26:35,620 --> 01:26:38,756
<b>I see it as an organism.</b>

2857
01:26:38,756 --> 01:26:40,925
<b>Everyone is just in different places,</b>

2858
01:26:40,925 --> 01:26:43,227
<b>doing different things at different times.</b>

2859
01:26:43,361 --> 01:26:44,796
<b>I always like to say,</b>

2860
01:26:44,796 --> 01:26:45,963
<b>"Brothers climbing a mountain,</b>

2861
01:26:45,963 --> 01:26:47,331
<b>each making their own effort."</b>

2862
01:26:47,532 --> 01:26:49,267
<b>Everyone doing their own thing.</b>

2863
01:26:49,267 --> 01:26:50,668
<b>No problem with that at all.</b>

2864
01:26:50,668 --> 01:26:52,603
<b>It's not a fight to the death.</b>

2865
01:26:53,171 --> 01:26:56,040
<b>LLMs don't conflict with what I want to do.</b>

2866
01:26:56,340 --> 01:26:59,277
<b>And without the recent developments in LLMs,</b>

2867
01:26:59,577 --> 01:27:00,478
<b>there might not have been</b>

2868
01:27:00,478 --> 01:27:02,847
<b>the current state of computer vision.</b>

2869
01:27:02,847 --> 01:27:03,648
<b>Mm.</b>

2870
01:27:03,815 --> 01:27:04,782
<b>That topic you discussed —</b>

2871
01:27:04,782 --> 01:27:06,584
<b>how to give AI the ability to love —</b>

2872
01:27:06,584 --> 01:27:08,219
<b>did you reach any conclusions?</b>

2873
01:27:09,220 --> 01:27:10,922
<b>The conclusion is that this is very important.</b>

2874
01:27:11,189 --> 01:27:11,989
<b>Why?</b>

2875
01:27:12,356 --> 01:27:14,225
<b>Because without it,</b>

2876
01:27:14,358 --> 01:27:17,962
<b>we face a very uncertain</b>

2877
01:27:17,962 --> 01:27:19,163
<b>and very dangerous future.</b>

2878
01:27:19,430 --> 01:27:21,732
<b>But with love comes hate.</b>

2879
01:27:21,966 --> 01:27:23,935
<b>They're two sides of the same coin.</b>

2880
01:27:23,935 --> 01:27:25,169
<b>It can't only have love.</b>

2881
01:27:25,169 --> 01:27:26,337
<b>When it learns to love,</b>

2882
01:27:26,337 --> 01:27:27,238
<b>it will definitely</b>

2883
01:27:27,238 --> 01:27:29,440
<b>know what the opposite is.</b>

2884
01:27:29,640 --> 01:27:30,474
<b>For me,</b>

2885
01:27:30,474 --> 01:27:31,809
<b>completely agree with you.</b>

2886
01:27:31,809 --> 01:27:32,610
<b>Mm.</b>

2887
01:27:32,977 --> 01:27:35,546
<b>This becomes a philosophical proposition.</b>

2888
01:27:35,546 --> 01:27:36,147
<b>Mm.</b>

2889
01:27:36,147 --> 01:27:39,584
<b>But let me ask a counter-question.</b>

2890
01:27:39,584 --> 01:27:43,187
<b>Why do people trust their own children,</b>

2891
01:27:43,387 --> 01:27:44,822
<b>trust humans so much,</b>

2892
01:27:45,556 --> 01:27:48,025
<b>but have such worry and fear</b>

2893
01:27:48,025 --> 01:27:49,660
<b>about AI, this new</b>

2894
01:27:49,861 --> 01:27:51,629
<b>form of intelligent entity?</b>

2895
01:27:51,896 --> 01:27:55,833
<b>I don't have an answer to that.</b>

2896
01:27:55,867 --> 01:27:56,434
<b>But I think</b>

2897
01:27:56,434 --> 01:27:58,202
<b>There will be technical ways</b>

2898
01:27:58,202 --> 01:28:01,839
<b>to have control.</b>

2899
01:28:02,173 --> 01:28:04,041
<b>We can use technical means</b>

2900
01:28:04,542 --> 01:28:07,612
<b>to make AI more trustworthy in the future,</b>

2901
01:28:07,612 --> 01:28:08,479
<b>safer,</b>

2902
01:28:08,479 --> 01:28:10,514
<b>and more controllable.</b>

2903
01:28:10,715 --> 01:28:11,816
<b>Mm. Controllable.</b>

2904
01:28:12,116 --> 01:28:14,919
<b>And this is also one reason</b>

2905
01:28:14,919 --> 01:28:15,653
<b>why we need to work on</b>

2906
01:28:15,653 --> 01:28:18,122
<b>world models.</b>

2907
01:28:18,589 --> 01:28:20,825
<b>Why did he want to reach out to you?</b>

2908
01:28:20,825 --> 01:28:21,359
<b>Uh, I don't know.</b>

2909
01:28:21,359 --> 01:28:22,860
<b>Maybe he reached out to</b>

2910
01:28:22,860 --> 01:28:23,394
<b>a thousand people,</b>

2911
01:28:23,394 --> 01:28:24,362
<b>ten thousand people.</b>

2912
01:28:24,996 --> 01:28:26,030
<b>I guess. Right.</b>

2913
01:28:27,231 --> 01:28:30,067
<b>When we were waiting in line at a restaurant that day,</b>

2914
01:28:30,067 --> 01:28:32,236
<b>we actually walked through the streets of New York together,</b>

2915
01:28:32,236 --> 01:28:34,805
<b>and our conversation naturally extended to</b>

2916
01:28:34,805 --> 01:28:37,141
<b>people who have greatly influenced you.</b>

2917
01:28:37,208 --> 01:28:39,043
<b>In what you shared just now,</b>

2918
01:28:39,043 --> 01:28:40,678
<b>the human factor</b>

2919
01:28:40,678 --> 01:28:43,781
<b>takes up a very large share of many of your choices.</b>

2920
01:28:44,348 --> 01:28:46,150
<b>Why are people so important to you?</b>

2921
01:28:46,150 --> 01:28:49,020
<b>And in your personal bio,</b>

2922
01:28:49,020 --> 01:28:51,322
<b>you clearly listed</b>

2923
01:28:51,322 --> 01:28:53,457
<b>which collaborators are important to you.</b>

2924
01:28:53,457 --> 01:28:54,625
<b>That's very rare.</b>

2925
01:28:54,625 --> 01:28:56,460
<b>Why are people so crucial to you?</b>

2926
01:28:56,627 --> 01:28:57,595
<b>Is this unusual?</b>

2927
01:28:57,595 --> 01:28:58,596
<b>I don't think it's unusual at all.</b>

2928
01:28:58,596 --> 01:28:59,997
<b>I think</b>

2929
01:28:59,997 --> 01:29:02,767
<b>In academic circles,</b>

2930
01:29:02,767 --> 01:29:05,736
<b>this is a common behavioral pattern.</b>

2931
01:29:05,736 --> 01:29:07,672
<b>People organize themselves into</b>

2932
01:29:07,672 --> 01:29:08,873
<b>these social networks.</b>

2933
01:29:08,873 --> 01:29:13,644
<b>Mm. And these people shape your thinking,</b>

2934
01:29:13,644 --> 01:29:15,179
<b>because they may be your students,</b>

2935
01:29:15,179 --> 01:29:17,214
<b>they may be your teachers, right?</b>

2936
01:29:17,214 --> 01:29:19,650
<b>But teachers don't always teach students.</b>

2937
01:29:19,650 --> 01:29:22,720
<b>Sometimes students teach the teachers.</b>

2938
01:29:22,720 --> 01:29:24,722
<b>All of this can be true.</b>

2939
01:29:24,722 --> 01:29:26,958
<b>So it's a huge graph</b>

2940
01:29:26,991 --> 01:29:29,593
<b>where everyone is connected.</b>

2941
01:29:29,593 --> 01:29:30,795
<b>And I think</b>

2942
01:29:30,795 --> 01:29:33,731
<b>That's also why research,</b>

2943
01:29:33,731 --> 01:29:35,967
<b>or science, is especially fascinating.</b>

2944
01:29:36,167 --> 01:29:38,169
<b>Mm. Because many times</b>

2945
01:29:38,235 --> 01:29:40,438
<b>the mutual</b>

2946
01:29:40,438 --> 01:29:41,772
<b>trust between people,</b>

2947
01:29:41,772 --> 01:29:43,474
<b>mutual appreciation,</b>

2948
01:29:43,474 --> 01:29:47,044
<b>mutual feelings —</b>

2949
01:29:47,078 --> 01:29:48,379
<b>these aren't built through</b>

2950
01:29:48,379 --> 01:29:49,714
<b>living together</b>

2951
01:29:49,714 --> 01:29:51,782
<b>and being friends.</b>

2952
01:29:51,782 --> 01:29:54,218
<b>Many times it's through scientific discovery,</b>

2953
01:29:54,218 --> 01:29:56,153
<b>kind of</b>

2954
01:29:56,153 --> 01:29:58,222
<b>this research aspect, that connections are built.</b>

2955
01:29:58,222 --> 01:29:59,423
<b>Relationships between people.</b>

2956
01:30:00,024 --> 01:30:01,859
<b>I think this is actually very interesting.</b>

2957
01:30:01,926 --> 01:30:04,161
<b>For example, those who deeply influenced me —</b>

2958
01:30:04,161 --> 01:30:07,531
<b>I may get to know them personally,</b>

2959
01:30:07,531 --> 01:30:09,633
<b>of course I try to get to know them personally,</b>

2960
01:30:09,633 --> 01:30:12,003
<b>right, but that's not what matters most to me.</b>

2961
01:30:12,003 --> 01:30:14,538
<b>I seem to understand them through their papers,</b>

2962
01:30:14,638 --> 01:30:15,873
<b>learning their way of thinking.</b>

2963
01:30:16,774 --> 01:30:17,641
<b>and</b>

2964
01:30:17,641 --> 01:30:19,377
<b>I think that's the real meaning of research.</b>

2965
01:30:19,610 --> 01:30:21,612
<b>I don't think the purpose of research is to publish papers.</b>

2966
01:30:21,612 --> 01:30:22,113
<b>I</b>

2967
01:30:22,113 --> 01:30:23,047
<b>I don't think</b>

2968
01:30:23,414 --> 01:30:24,215
<b>Uh,</b>

2969
01:30:24,448 --> 01:30:25,216
<b>publishing papers</b>

2970
01:30:25,216 --> 01:30:28,052
<b>is the goal.</b>

2971
01:30:28,052 --> 01:30:29,120
<b>Not at all.</b>

2972
01:30:29,320 --> 01:30:30,221
<b>The purpose should be —</b>

2973
01:30:31,122 --> 01:30:32,390
<b>what is the purpose?</b>

2974
01:30:32,390 --> 01:30:33,190
<b>ah,</b>

2975
01:30:33,557 --> 01:30:36,027
<b>Is it a journey through people?</b>

2976
01:30:36,594 --> 01:30:39,263
<b>What Kaiming told me the purpose is:</b>

2977
01:30:40,164 --> 01:30:40,965
<b>Mm.</b>

2978
01:30:41,399 --> 01:30:44,034
<b>at its core it means</b>

2979
01:30:44,435 --> 01:30:45,970
<b>sharing knowledge.</b>

2980
01:30:46,537 --> 01:30:50,641
<b>that is,</b>
<b>The purpose of publishing a paper isn't for others to see it,</b>

2981
01:30:51,542 --> 01:30:54,045
<b>but so that after others see the paper,</b>

2982
01:30:54,045 --> 01:30:55,179
<b>they have something to work on.</b>

2983
01:30:56,947 --> 01:30:57,715
<b>that is,</b>

2984
01:30:57,715 --> 01:30:59,216
<b>You publish a paper,</b>

2985
01:30:59,350 --> 01:31:01,018
<b>others understand some of the content,</b>

2986
01:31:01,018 --> 01:31:02,019
<b>and they feel</b>

2987
01:31:02,019 --> 01:31:04,388
<b>their own horizons have expanded.</b>

2988
01:31:04,588 --> 01:31:06,357
<b>Mm. It's about helping others.</b>

2989
01:31:06,357 --> 01:31:07,425
<b>Being helpful to others.</b>

2990
01:31:07,525 --> 01:31:09,026
<b>Right. Being able to inspire others,</b>

2991
01:31:09,026 --> 01:31:10,261
<b>or enlighten others.</b>

2992
01:31:10,261 --> 01:31:12,263
<b>Oh, that's the purpose of research.</b>

2993
01:31:12,563 --> 01:31:14,198
<b>I think that's the purpose of research.</b>

2994
01:31:14,198 --> 01:31:15,966
<b>Or, to put it more romantically,</b>

2995
01:31:15,966 --> 01:31:17,468
<b>the idea is</b>

2996
01:31:17,468 --> 01:31:20,805
<b>I think this —</b>
<b>this comes from Hannah Arendt (political philosopher),</b>

2997
01:31:21,005 --> 01:31:23,441
<b>and she said</b>

2998
01:31:23,641 --> 01:31:25,576
<b>she doesn't care about impact.</b>

2999
01:31:25,676 --> 01:31:27,578
<b>She doesn't care about influence.</b>

3000
01:31:27,645 --> 01:31:28,045
<b>Because</b>

3001
01:31:28,045 --> 01:31:29,447
<b>In researcher circles,</b>

3002
01:31:29,447 --> 01:31:30,147
<b>people say</b>

3003
01:31:30,147 --> 01:31:33,317
<b>we publish papers to create some kind of impact,</b>

3004
01:31:33,317 --> 01:31:33,918
<b>Right?</b>

3005
01:31:33,918 --> 01:31:35,019
<b>In my own dictionary,</b>

3006
01:31:35,019 --> 01:31:37,621
<b>I actually have a bit of an aversion to the word impact.</b>

3007
01:31:37,755 --> 01:31:38,456
<b>Aversion.</b>

3008
01:31:38,456 --> 01:31:39,356
<b>A bit of an aversion.</b>

3009
01:31:39,356 --> 01:31:40,257
<b>Oh.</b>

3010
01:31:40,858 --> 01:31:41,826
<b>Uh, why?</b>

3011
01:31:41,826 --> 01:31:43,327
<b>What is it about it that you resist?</b>

3012
01:31:43,627 --> 01:31:44,762
<b>Again, Arendt</b>

3013
01:31:44,762 --> 01:31:45,729
<b>said that</b>

3014
01:31:45,729 --> 01:31:47,798
<b>she felt, uh,</b>

3015
01:31:47,798 --> 01:31:51,535
<b>the word "impact" is overly aggressive,</b>

3016
01:31:51,535 --> 01:31:53,170
<b>overly masculine.</b>

3017
01:31:54,071 --> 01:31:55,473
<b>For her,</b>

3018
01:31:55,473 --> 01:31:58,642
<b>the purpose of doing these things is not to create impact</b>

3019
01:31:58,809 --> 01:32:00,644
<b>but for understanding itself.</b>

3020
01:32:01,378 --> 01:32:03,848
<b>If you can understand something,</b>

3021
01:32:03,948 --> 01:32:05,983
<b>the feeling is wonderful.</b>

3022
01:32:06,784 --> 01:32:09,820
<b>If you can write down what you've understood,</b>

3023
01:32:09,854 --> 01:32:12,223
<b>whether it's an article or a paper,</b>

3024
01:32:12,389 --> 01:32:13,524
<b>and spread it,</b>

3025
01:32:13,824 --> 01:32:14,558
<b>then you can</b>

3026
01:32:14,558 --> 01:32:16,961
<b>potentially allow more people in the world</b>

3027
01:32:17,361 --> 01:32:18,629
<b>to understand</b>

3028
01:32:18,629 --> 01:32:21,365
<b>such a question in the same way you do.</b>

3029
01:32:21,465 --> 01:32:23,734
<b>And this</b>

3030
01:32:23,734 --> 01:32:26,437
<b>will be transmitted step by step,</b>

3031
01:32:26,437 --> 01:32:30,174
<b>creating a kind of resonance.</b>

3032
01:32:30,341 --> 01:32:30,674
<b>and</b>

3033
01:32:30,674 --> 01:32:32,943
<b>Arendt's view is that</b>

3034
01:32:33,144 --> 01:32:35,713
<b>she would find in this a sense of family —</b>

3035
01:32:35,713 --> 01:32:36,780
<b>a feeling of family.</b>

3036
01:32:37,448 --> 01:32:40,251
<b>She would feel that she understood something,</b>

3037
01:32:40,851 --> 01:32:41,785
<b>told others,</b>

3038
01:32:41,785 --> 01:32:43,254
<b>allowed others to understand,</b>

3039
01:32:43,721 --> 01:32:46,924
<b>which means these people also understood her to some degree.</b>

3040
01:32:47,358 --> 01:32:47,958
<b>Mm.</b>

3041
01:32:47,958 --> 01:32:50,261
<b>But humans, as social beings,</b>

3042
01:32:50,361 --> 01:32:51,629
<b>need to be understood.</b>

3043
01:32:51,962 --> 01:32:52,530
<b>Right.</b>

3044
01:32:52,530 --> 01:32:53,797
<b>He reframed the word "influence"</b>

3045
01:32:53,797 --> 01:32:56,734
<b>in a very soft way —</b>

3046
01:32:56,734 --> 01:32:58,068
<b>seeking to be understood.</b>

3047
01:32:58,202 --> 01:32:59,436
<b>I think so.</b>

3048
01:32:59,436 --> 01:33:00,137
<b>I think so.</b>

3049
01:33:00,137 --> 01:33:01,472
<b>You agree more with this view?</b>

3050
01:33:01,472 --> 01:33:03,407
<b>I agree with her very much.</b>

3051
01:33:03,474 --> 01:33:05,543
<b>Because I think</b>

3052
01:33:05,543 --> 01:33:08,245
<b>Creating impact is fine in itself.</b>

3053
01:33:08,245 --> 01:33:09,747
<b>But it's very self-centered.</b>

3054
01:33:09,747 --> 01:33:11,182
<b>Mm-hmm.</b>

3055
01:33:11,182 --> 01:33:12,917
<b>I'm going to create impact. Mm.</b>

3056
01:33:12,917 --> 01:33:14,218
<b>Right. Me-centered.</b>

3057
01:33:14,218 --> 01:33:15,786
<b>And yes,</b>

3058
01:33:15,786 --> 01:33:16,854
<b>you're absolutely right.</b>

3059
01:33:16,854 --> 01:33:18,422
<b>I'm going to create this impact,</b>

3060
01:33:18,589 --> 01:33:20,157
<b>I'm going to change the world,</b>

3061
01:33:21,225 --> 01:33:25,362
<b>but do the people in this world agree to be changed by me?</b>

3062
01:33:25,763 --> 01:33:26,564
<b>[laughs]</b>

3063
01:33:26,797 --> 01:33:28,732
<b>Or rather, many disasters in the world</b>

3064
01:33:28,732 --> 01:33:31,468
<b>are because people want to create impact,</b>

3065
01:33:31,468 --> 01:33:34,805
<b>want to transform the world.</b>

3066
01:33:34,805 --> 01:33:35,206
<b>Right.</b>

3067
01:33:35,206 --> 01:33:36,373
<b>I think</b>

3068
01:33:36,373 --> 01:33:40,044
<b>I would tend to agree with this softer expression.</b>

3069
01:33:40,044 --> 01:33:41,812
<b>I think</b>

3070
01:33:41,812 --> 01:33:45,316
<b>If all people in this world,</b>

3071
01:33:45,316 --> 01:33:47,218
<b>through our research,</b>

3072
01:33:47,218 --> 01:33:49,520
<b>can gain a new layer of understanding,</b>

3073
01:33:49,520 --> 01:33:52,122
<b>a new layer of knowledge,</b>

3074
01:33:52,122 --> 01:33:55,259
<b>the total intelligence on Earth would increase.</b>

3075
01:33:55,559 --> 01:33:58,429
<b>And increasing total intelligence on Earth</b>

3076
01:33:58,429 --> 01:33:59,930
<b>is never wrong.</b>

3077
01:34:00,831 --> 01:34:03,834
<b>It's always something beneficial to the world.</b>

3078
01:34:04,068 --> 01:34:05,769
<b>Whether it's called impact</b>

3079
01:34:05,769 --> 01:34:08,138
<b>or being understood by more people.</b>

3080
01:34:08,138 --> 01:34:11,942
<b>Do you want to be known and remembered by more people?</b>

3081
01:34:12,042 --> 01:34:15,279
<b>Mm. Do you have a need for fame?</b>

3082
01:34:15,379 --> 01:34:16,647
<b>I certainly don't have that need.</b>

3083
01:34:16,647 --> 01:34:17,715
<b>You don't have that need.</b>

3084
01:34:17,715 --> 01:34:18,148
<b>But I think</b>

3085
01:34:18,148 --> 01:34:19,416
<b>I don't have that need.</b>

3086
01:34:19,416 --> 01:34:20,251
<b>But really?</b>

3087
01:34:20,351 --> 01:34:21,185
<b>Uh, I</b>

3088
01:34:21,185 --> 01:34:23,721
<b>Or rather, from where I stand now,</b>

3089
01:34:23,854 --> 01:34:26,390
<b>I'm actually a victim</b>

3090
01:34:26,390 --> 01:34:27,358
<b>of a kind of false fame.</b>

3091
01:34:28,325 --> 01:34:29,426
<b>Uh, the reason is</b>

3092
01:34:29,426 --> 01:34:32,029
<b>people now take some of our papers</b>

3093
01:34:32,029 --> 01:34:33,631
<b>and post them on Xiaohongshu,</b>

3094
01:34:33,631 --> 01:34:37,334
<b>to discuss — and actually none of this</b>

3095
01:34:37,334 --> 01:34:39,270
<b>— people talk about the so-called top-three conferences</b>

3096
01:34:39,270 --> 01:34:41,538
<b>and promote the work, right?</b>

3097
01:34:42,306 --> 01:34:44,008
<b>I</b>
<b>I have never once</b>

3098
01:34:44,008 --> 01:34:47,177
<b>asked any such media outlet</b>

3099
01:34:47,411 --> 01:34:48,879
<b>to do this kind of promotion.</b>

3100
01:34:48,879 --> 01:34:49,813
<b>Mm.</b>

3101
01:34:49,813 --> 01:34:51,849
<b>And I tell my students:</b>

3102
01:34:51,849 --> 01:34:54,151
<b>please don't go on Xiaohongshu</b>

3103
01:34:54,151 --> 01:34:55,219
<b>or Zhihu</b>

3104
01:34:55,519 --> 01:34:56,987
<b>to promote your own work.</b>

3105
01:34:56,987 --> 01:34:58,122
<b>You can explain your work,</b>

3106
01:34:58,122 --> 01:34:59,556
<b>you can comment on your work.</b>

3107
01:34:59,556 --> 01:35:00,591
<b>That's fine.</b>

3108
01:35:00,591 --> 01:35:02,026
<b>Just don't promote yourself.</b>

3109
01:35:02,026 --> 01:35:03,827
<b>Why is it okay on X?</b>

3110
01:35:04,194 --> 01:35:05,929
<b>I think on X,</b>

3111
01:35:06,363 --> 01:35:09,166
<b>uh, it's more about</b>

3112
01:35:09,166 --> 01:35:10,868
<b>how you define promotion.</b>

3113
01:35:10,868 --> 01:35:12,436
<b>What I focus on</b>

3114
01:35:12,436 --> 01:35:15,839
<b>is briefly summarizing things</b>

3115
01:35:15,839 --> 01:35:17,474
<b>and telling people what it's about.</b>

3116
01:35:17,574 --> 01:35:20,077
<b>It's more like attracting people to look at my work,</b>

3117
01:35:20,077 --> 01:35:21,445
<b>and I think that's fine.</b>

3118
01:35:21,445 --> 01:35:22,346
<b>But the promotion I'm referring to</b>

3119
01:35:22,346 --> 01:35:24,982
<b>is more like the fame you mentioned,</b>

3120
01:35:24,982 --> 01:35:27,651
<b>because what I really can't accept is</b>

3121
01:35:27,651 --> 01:35:31,789
<b>people now say "so-and-so's team"</b>

3122
01:35:31,789 --> 01:35:32,122
<b>published such-and-such</b>

3123
01:35:32,122 --> 01:35:32,856
<b>work.</b>

3124
01:35:32,856 --> 01:35:33,657
<b>Oh.</b>

3125
01:35:33,824 --> 01:35:35,125
<b>It reinforces that person,</b>

3126
01:35:35,125 --> 01:35:35,993
<b>reinforcing that person,</b>

3127
01:35:35,993 --> 01:35:37,027
<b>someone's team.</b>

3128
01:35:37,027 --> 01:35:37,861
<b>reinforces that person.</b>

3129
01:35:37,861 --> 01:35:38,729
<b>Right, uh,</b>

3130
01:35:38,729 --> 01:35:41,598
<b>If any editors hear this,</b>

3131
01:35:41,632 --> 01:35:44,968
<b>I hope people can stop doing this.</b>

3132
01:35:44,968 --> 01:35:46,270
<b>Don't write "Xie Saining's team".</b>

3133
01:35:46,270 --> 01:35:47,971
<b>Don't put my photo on it.</b>

3134
01:35:47,971 --> 01:35:49,606
<b>Don't put my name on it.</b>

3135
01:35:49,940 --> 01:35:52,476
<b>We need to encourage young people more —</b>

3136
01:35:52,476 --> 01:35:54,878
<b>the people who actually did the work,</b>

3137
01:35:55,212 --> 01:35:57,014
<b>give them more visibility.</b>

3138
01:35:57,214 --> 01:35:57,715
<b>Right?</b>

3139
01:35:57,715 --> 01:35:59,983
<b>Well, people might think you're the first author.</b>

3140
01:35:59,983 --> 01:36:00,384
<b>Uh, right.</b>

3141
01:36:00,384 --> 01:36:01,819
<b>If I am the first author, that's fine.</b>

3142
01:36:01,819 --> 01:36:02,720
<b>But I'm not the first author.</b>

3143
01:36:02,720 --> 01:36:03,554
<b>Right?</b>

3144
01:36:03,554 --> 01:36:05,556
<b>I'm just the team lead.</b>

3145
01:36:05,622 --> 01:36:08,625
<b>And much of this work is done by students.</b>

3146
01:36:08,792 --> 01:36:10,227
<b>So what should it be called?</b>

3147
01:36:10,861 --> 01:36:12,196
<b>Not "Xie Saining's team".</b>

3148
01:36:12,529 --> 01:36:13,630
<b>Just focus on the work itself.</b>

3149
01:36:14,598 --> 01:36:18,202
<b>Talk about what problem this solves</b>

3150
01:36:18,202 --> 01:36:20,070
<b>and why it matters.</b>

3151
01:36:20,070 --> 01:36:21,038
<b>That's enough.</b>

3152
01:36:21,238 --> 01:36:21,972
<b>Right.</b>

3153
01:36:21,972 --> 01:36:22,439
<b>But I think</b>

3154
01:36:22,439 --> 01:36:24,742
<b>You really hate being used as a target by others.</b>

3155
01:36:24,742 --> 01:36:25,542
<b>Is that so?</b>

3156
01:36:25,743 --> 01:36:26,677
<b>Uh, yes.</b>

3157
01:36:26,677 --> 01:36:29,179
<b>Because I think it adds</b>

3158
01:36:29,179 --> 01:36:30,848
<b>a lot of risk.</b>

3159
01:36:30,914 --> 01:36:32,983
<b>I think</b>

3160
01:36:32,983 --> 01:36:35,919
<b>Mm. Tell us about those who influenced you.</b>

3161
01:36:35,919 --> 01:36:37,788
<b>We've already talked about a few people.</b>

3162
01:36:37,788 --> 01:36:39,923
<b>Kaiming, Professor Tu — anyone else?</b>

3163
01:36:39,923 --> 01:36:40,758
<b>Oh, yes.</b>

3164
01:36:40,758 --> 01:36:41,558
<b>Uh,</b>

3165
01:36:41,992 --> 01:36:43,961
<b>I think, right,</b>

3166
01:36:43,961 --> 01:36:44,428
<b>this goes</b>

3167
01:36:44,428 --> 01:36:45,662
<b>back to FAIR.</b>

3168
01:36:45,662 --> 01:36:47,030
<b>We can follow the FAIR thread.</b>

3169
01:36:47,030 --> 01:36:49,233
<b>After FAIR,</b>

3170
01:36:49,566 --> 01:36:50,768
<b>I came to NYU.</b>

3171
01:36:50,768 --> 01:36:53,003
<b>I think this was another decision-making point.</b>

3172
01:36:53,871 --> 01:36:55,372
<b>Stayed at FAIR for 4 years.</b>

3173
01:36:55,372 --> 01:36:56,373
<b>A full 4 years.</b>

3174
01:36:56,540 --> 01:36:57,474
<b>Right. OK.</b>

3175
01:36:57,474 --> 01:36:59,443
<b>Yes. Yes.</b>

3176
01:36:59,443 --> 01:37:00,577
<b>Also with ups and downs.</b>

3177
01:37:00,577 --> 01:37:01,178
<b>For me,</b>

3178
01:37:01,178 --> 01:37:01,879
<b>I just said</b>

3179
01:37:01,879 --> 01:37:03,313
<b>many places I've been</b>

3180
01:37:03,313 --> 01:37:05,582
<b>actually grew alongside me.</b>

3181
01:37:05,582 --> 01:37:07,451
<b>FAIR might be an exception.</b>

3182
01:37:07,451 --> 01:37:08,619
<b>When I joined, it was at its peak.</b>

3183
01:37:08,619 --> 01:37:09,720
<b>The high point.</b>

3184
01:37:09,720 --> 01:37:10,821
<b>Probably the high point.</b>

3185
01:37:10,821 --> 01:37:12,389
<b>Right. And then</b>

3186
01:37:12,389 --> 01:37:14,391
<b>Right. It's a pity.</b>

3187
01:37:14,391 --> 01:37:16,860
<b>What's happening there now.</b>

3188
01:37:17,261 --> 01:37:17,928
<b>But I also think</b>

3189
01:37:17,928 --> 01:37:18,729
<b>Mm.</b>

3190
01:37:18,929 --> 01:37:20,998
<b>Right. Because I left relatively early,</b>

3191
01:37:20,998 --> 01:37:22,065
<b>so I wasn't there</b>

3192
01:37:22,232 --> 01:37:23,867
<b>when it was</b>

3193
01:37:23,867 --> 01:37:26,003
<b>at its lowest point when I left.</b>

3194
01:37:26,003 --> 01:37:27,037
<b>Right. [laughs]</b>

3195
01:37:27,037 --> 01:37:29,339
<b>I also saw some warning signs.</b>

3196
01:37:29,473 --> 01:37:29,807
<b>Right.</b>

3197
01:37:29,807 --> 01:37:30,474
<b>OK.</b>

3198
01:37:30,474 --> 01:37:33,343
<b>And, but, right.</b>

3199
01:37:33,343 --> 01:37:34,178
<b>And I think</b>

3200
01:37:34,178 --> 01:37:35,712
<b>if I'm talking about people who influenced me,</b>

3201
01:37:35,712 --> 01:37:38,015
<b>then in this process, when going to NYU,</b>

3202
01:37:38,048 --> 01:37:41,251
<b>I think</b>
<b>that was another quite mysterious decision-making process.</b>

3203
01:37:41,518 --> 01:37:45,789
<b>Right. Deciding to go to New York at that time</b>

3204
01:37:45,789 --> 01:37:46,757
<b>— I just mentioned this —</b>

3205
01:37:46,757 --> 01:37:49,359
<b>was partly because I might enjoy the city.</b>

3206
01:37:49,793 --> 01:37:50,360
<b>and</b>

3207
01:37:50,360 --> 01:37:51,395
<b>But I think</b>

3208
01:37:51,428 --> 01:37:52,663
<b>Uh, another very important thing</b>

3209
01:37:52,663 --> 01:37:54,465
<b>was also that Yann LeCun is here.</b>

3210
01:37:54,465 --> 01:37:55,632
<b>Right, Yann is here.</b>

3211
01:37:55,766 --> 01:37:58,068
<b>Mm, right, uh.</b>

3212
01:37:58,435 --> 01:37:59,536
<b>Why, with him here,</b>

3213
01:37:59,536 --> 01:38:00,437
<b>were you willing to go?</b>

3214
01:38:00,571 --> 01:38:02,072
<b>You worked together at FAIR.</b>

3215
01:38:02,372 --> 01:38:03,173
<b>Uh,</b>

3216
01:38:03,474 --> 01:38:06,610
<b>He likes to say he's recruited me</b>

3217
01:38:06,610 --> 01:38:07,845
<b>that is,</b>

3218
01:38:07,845 --> 01:38:09,446
<b>three times, right?</b>

3219
01:38:09,713 --> 01:38:11,748
<b>The first time was at FAIR.</b>

3220
01:38:11,748 --> 01:38:12,216
<b>But at that time,</b>

3221
01:38:12,216 --> 01:38:14,585
<b>because he was the overall director of FAIR,</b>

3222
01:38:14,585 --> 01:38:16,620
<b>FAIR's director,</b>

3223
01:38:16,620 --> 01:38:18,722
<b>I didn't directly work with him,</b>

3224
01:38:18,722 --> 01:38:20,624
<b>but I was influenced by him of course.</b>

3225
01:38:20,958 --> 01:38:22,960
<b>Or have you had long-term exchanges?</b>

3226
01:38:23,026 --> 01:38:24,127
<b>Yes, we've talked.</b>

3227
01:38:24,127 --> 01:38:24,928
<b>Right.</b>

3228
01:38:25,395 --> 01:38:26,763
<b>But never directly collaborated.</b>

3229
01:38:26,930 --> 01:38:27,731
<b>Mm.</b>

3230
01:38:27,865 --> 01:38:30,133
<b>Then going to NYU was the second time.</b>

3231
01:38:30,133 --> 01:38:31,668
<b>We can talk about the third time later.</b>

3232
01:38:32,135 --> 01:38:33,003
<b>Mm.</b>

3233
01:38:33,470 --> 01:38:36,640
<b>And the NYU experience —</b>

3234
01:38:36,640 --> 01:38:39,243
<b>I think why it matters that he's here</b>

3235
01:38:39,243 --> 01:38:39,743
<b>is also because</b>

3236
01:38:39,743 --> 01:38:42,980
<b>I think</b>
<b>he's a person with a very strong vision.</b>

3237
01:38:43,580 --> 01:38:44,648
<b>so</b>

3238
01:38:45,749 --> 01:38:46,116
<b>Right.</b>

3239
01:38:46,116 --> 01:38:48,752
<b>I think many of these decisions were very intuitive.</b>

3240
01:38:48,752 --> 01:38:50,754
<b>For example, NYU's building,</b>

3241
01:38:50,754 --> 01:38:53,457
<b>which we call the Center for Data Science,</b>

3242
01:38:53,457 --> 01:38:56,159
<b>the so-called Data Science Center,</b>

3243
01:38:56,159 --> 01:38:59,263
<b>this was actually led by Yann</b>

3244
01:38:59,263 --> 01:39:00,831
<b>over ten years ago.</b>

3245
01:39:01,064 --> 01:39:03,600
<b>He established this organization.</b>

3246
01:39:03,734 --> 01:39:06,036
<b>Right. It's independent of</b>

3247
01:39:06,036 --> 01:39:07,471
<b>traditional computer science departments</b>

3248
01:39:07,471 --> 01:39:08,805
<b>or math departments.</b>

3249
01:39:08,805 --> 01:39:11,541
<b>It's a new department.</b>

3250
01:39:12,175 --> 01:39:13,610
<b>So we have a new building,</b>

3251
01:39:13,677 --> 01:39:15,812
<b>and the first time I walked into this building,</b>

3252
01:39:15,812 --> 01:39:17,648
<b>I felt great.</b>

3253
01:39:17,648 --> 01:39:18,649
<b>Because</b>

3254
01:39:18,649 --> 01:39:20,250
<b>Everything is glass doors.</b>

3255
01:39:20,250 --> 01:39:22,352
<b>Right.</b>
<b>I can take you to see it sometime.</b>

3256
01:39:22,352 --> 01:39:24,221
<b>All glass doors.</b>

3257
01:39:24,221 --> 01:39:26,023
<b>Uh, everything is very, very open.</b>

3258
01:39:26,189 --> 01:39:27,591
<b>And it feels a bit like a company for students.</b>

3259
01:39:27,591 --> 01:39:29,960
<b>And the color scheme is very nice.</b>

3260
01:39:29,960 --> 01:39:31,595
<b>Right, I keep saying I'm a visual person.</b>

3261
01:39:31,595 --> 01:39:34,464
<b>There are warm tones in there,</b>

3262
01:39:34,464 --> 01:39:37,434
<b>with an orange floor,</b>

3263
01:39:37,434 --> 01:39:38,568
<b>various sofas,</b>

3264
01:39:38,568 --> 01:39:39,803
<b>and everyone, uh,</b>

3265
01:39:39,803 --> 01:39:41,405
<b>though it's quite chaotic —</b>

3266
01:39:41,405 --> 01:39:42,573
<b>all kinds of robots</b>

3267
01:39:42,573 --> 01:39:44,575
<b>running around on the floor,</b>

3268
01:39:44,575 --> 01:39:46,843
<b>various students on this sofa,</b>

3269
01:39:46,843 --> 01:39:47,678
<b>that sofa,</b>

3270
01:39:47,678 --> 01:39:49,179
<b>sitting and studying.</b>

3271
01:39:49,446 --> 01:39:50,981
<b>And there's absolutely no privacy —</b>

3272
01:39:50,981 --> 01:39:52,349
<b>zero privacy.</b>

3273
01:39:52,382 --> 01:39:54,918
<b>All the professors' office glass doors —</b>

3274
01:39:54,918 --> 01:39:57,020
<b>you can see clearly everything happening inside.</b>

3275
01:39:57,020 --> 01:39:57,955
<b>Mm. Right.</b>

3276
01:39:58,055 --> 01:39:58,956
<b>But I thought, wow,</b>

3277
01:39:58,956 --> 01:40:00,457
<b>this is very interesting.</b>

3278
01:40:00,457 --> 01:40:01,725
<b>This environment is very interesting.</b>

3279
01:40:01,992 --> 01:40:03,126
<b>Right.</b>

3280
01:40:03,126 --> 01:40:05,929
<b>More and more American schools now</b>

3281
01:40:05,929 --> 01:40:07,931
<b>are making efforts like this,</b>

3282
01:40:07,931 --> 01:40:09,733
<b>saying we want to have</b>

3283
01:40:10,400 --> 01:40:12,169
<b>mm, this kind of</b>

3284
01:40:12,469 --> 01:40:13,937
<b>uh, interdisciplinary</b>

3285
01:40:13,937 --> 01:40:15,973
<b>cross-disciplinary centers.</b>

3286
01:40:15,973 --> 01:40:17,040
