3358
01:42:30,073 --> 01:42:33,477
<b>her journey wasn't smooth sailing at all.</b>

3359
01:42:33,477 --> 01:42:37,614
<b>Mm. She also had to</b>

3360
01:42:38,582 --> 01:42:39,950
<b>wade through many thorns,</b>

3361
01:42:39,950 --> 01:42:42,753
<b>overcoming many obstacles step by step,</b>

3362
01:42:42,853 --> 01:42:43,987
<b>and now</b>

3363
01:42:44,154 --> 01:42:46,590
<b>standing on the world stage,</b>

3364
01:42:46,756 --> 01:42:48,325
<b>becoming a pride of the Chinese community,</b>

3365
01:42:48,325 --> 01:42:51,194
<b>or becoming a North Star for the entire research field,</b>

3366
01:42:51,194 --> 01:42:54,431
<b>especially computer vision,</b>

3367
01:42:54,664 --> 01:42:57,634
<b>allowing everyone to see</b>

3368
01:42:57,634 --> 01:43:01,238
<b>what she's thinking</b>

3369
01:43:01,238 --> 01:43:02,973
<b>and being able to</b>

3370
01:43:02,973 --> 01:43:04,207
<b>in some sense</b>

3371
01:43:04,941 --> 01:43:07,077
<b>set some new directions.</b>

3372
01:43:07,077 --> 01:43:09,412
<b>I think</b>

3373
01:43:09,579 --> 01:43:11,381
<b>Right, her influence on me has been enormous.</b>

3374
01:43:11,615 --> 01:43:12,048
<b>Mm.</b>

3375
01:43:12,048 --> 01:43:12,716
<b>and</b>

3376
01:43:12,716 --> 01:43:15,919
<b>And I think Professor Fei-Fei's greatest strength is</b>

3377
01:43:15,919 --> 01:43:19,156
<b>that she's someone who can define problems.</b>

3378
01:43:19,356 --> 01:43:20,323
<b>Mm. This point</b>

3379
01:43:20,323 --> 01:43:22,993
<b>is actually not very intuitive.</b>

3380
01:43:22,993 --> 01:43:27,230
<b>When people talk about Professor Fei-Fei,</b>

3381
01:43:27,264 --> 01:43:29,399
<b>her greatest achievement</b>

3382
01:43:29,399 --> 01:43:30,800
<b>is building ImageNet,</b>

3383
01:43:30,800 --> 01:43:31,868
<b>this dataset.</b>

3384
01:43:32,469 --> 01:43:34,805
<b>But in fact, this isn't just a dataset.</b>

3385
01:43:34,805 --> 01:43:37,874
<b>This isn't just data.</b>

3386
01:43:37,874 --> 01:43:39,409
<b>It's hard to imagine</b>

3387
01:43:39,409 --> 01:43:41,811
<b>that back then, right,</b>

3388
01:43:41,811 --> 01:43:45,215
<b>around 2012 or 2011,</b>

3389
01:43:46,049 --> 01:43:49,653
<b>image classification wasn't a well-defined problem.</b>

3390
01:43:49,653 --> 01:43:51,988
<b>Defining this problem clearly</b>

3391
01:43:51,988 --> 01:43:53,557
<b>was far more important</b>

3392
01:43:53,557 --> 01:43:54,524
<b>than building such a dataset —</b>

3393
01:43:54,524 --> 01:43:55,959
<b>far, far more important.</b>

3394
01:43:55,959 --> 01:43:57,060
<b>Mm-hmm.</b>

3395
01:43:57,561 --> 01:43:59,996
<b>And I think Professor Fei-Fei</b>

3396
01:43:59,996 --> 01:44:01,531
<b>set this agenda,</b>

3397
01:44:01,531 --> 01:44:03,133
<b>defined this problem clearly,</b>

3398
01:44:03,133 --> 01:44:04,935
<b>so that subsequently</b>

3399
01:44:04,935 --> 01:44:07,070
<b>Deep Learning could have a playground,</b>

3400
01:44:07,070 --> 01:44:08,772
<b>have such a platform</b>

3401
01:44:08,772 --> 01:44:10,207
<b>to showcase its capabilities.</b>

3402
01:44:10,340 --> 01:44:11,074
<b>I think</b>

3403
01:44:11,074 --> 01:44:12,809
<b>This is her greatest achievement,</b>

3404
01:44:12,809 --> 01:44:14,644
<b>and also what I always want to learn from.</b>

3405
01:44:14,778 --> 01:44:15,412
<b>Mm. Right.</b>

3406
01:44:15,412 --> 01:44:16,980
<b>So I worked with her on</b>

3407
01:44:16,980 --> 01:44:17,747
<b>two pieces of work.</b>

3408
01:44:17,747 --> 01:44:19,049
<b>One is Thinking Space,</b>

3409
01:44:19,049 --> 01:44:19,916
<b>and</b>

3410
01:44:19,916 --> 01:44:20,617
<b>this paper</b>

3411
01:44:20,617 --> 01:44:22,319
<b>mainly involves</b>

3412
01:44:22,319 --> 01:44:24,120
<b>within multimodal base models,</b>

3413
01:44:24,120 --> 01:44:25,555
<b>how to solve,</b>

3414
01:44:25,555 --> 01:44:27,357
<b>better solve this kind of</b>

3415
01:44:27,357 --> 01:44:29,426
<b>uh, spatial intelligence problem.</b>

3416
01:44:30,160 --> 01:44:33,330
<b>Well, recently we have another paper called Cambrian-S,</b>

3417
01:44:33,430 --> 01:44:35,765
<b>and this paper also addresses</b>

3418
01:44:35,765 --> 01:44:38,468
<b>questions about video —</b>

3419
01:44:38,468 --> 01:44:40,637
<b>how do we define problems,</b>

3420
01:44:40,637 --> 01:44:42,272
<b>which problems are actually important.</b>

3421
01:44:42,572 --> 01:44:43,373
<b>Right.</b>

3422
01:44:43,373 --> 01:44:46,610
<b>I think this collaboration with her</b>

3423
01:44:46,643 --> 01:44:48,778
<b>has also helped expand the boundaries of my research.</b>

3424
01:44:49,279 --> 01:44:51,781
<b>How did you come to know Professor Fei-Fei well?</b>

3425
01:44:52,182 --> 01:44:54,050
<b>Uh, it was all quite serendipitous.</b>

3426
01:44:54,050 --> 01:44:55,785
<b>She came to New York on a business trip once,</b>

3427
01:44:55,785 --> 01:44:58,355
<b>and we had a meal together.</b>

3428
01:44:58,788 --> 01:45:00,056
<b>And she told me</b>

3429
01:45:00,056 --> 01:45:01,558
<b>a lot of things.</b>

3430
01:45:01,758 --> 01:45:05,028
<b>Right. And she would often come to New York later,</b>

3431
01:45:05,028 --> 01:45:07,163
<b>and because she's also starting a company,</b>

3432
01:45:07,163 --> 01:45:08,732
<b>we would often get together</b>

3433
01:45:08,732 --> 01:45:09,599
<b>and chat.</b>

3434
01:45:09,799 --> 01:45:10,867
<b>Right, roughly that.</b>

3435
01:45:10,934 --> 01:45:12,869
<b>And normally we'd have</b>

3436
01:45:12,869 --> 01:45:13,770
<b>some research meetings.</b>

3437
01:45:14,671 --> 01:45:16,273
<b>Mm. I'm curious about something,</b>

3438
01:45:16,273 --> 01:45:19,276
<b>and I think many people are curious about this too.</b>

3439
01:45:19,276 --> 01:45:24,714
<b>Mm.</b>
<b>How did you go from being a very young</b>

3440
01:45:24,948 --> 01:45:27,784
<b>researcher just starting out in academia,</b>

3441
01:45:27,784 --> 01:45:28,518
<b>and gradually,</b>

3442
01:45:28,518 --> 01:45:31,922
<b>come to be alongside these well-known names in AI,</b>

3443
01:45:31,922 --> 01:45:32,622
<b>come together with them</b>

3444
01:45:32,622 --> 01:45:34,057
<b>and stand alongside them?</b>

3445
01:45:34,057 --> 01:45:34,524
<b>That is,</b>

3446
01:45:34,524 --> 01:45:37,761
<b>how did you enter the core of AI?</b>

3447
01:45:39,329 --> 01:45:40,030
<b>I</b>

3448
01:45:40,030 --> 01:45:41,731
<b>I still don't feel I'm at the core of AI,</b>

3449
01:45:41,731 --> 01:45:44,034
<b>or that I've gotten close to it.</b>

3450
01:45:44,034 --> 01:45:45,635
<b>Mm. But the people you just mentioned,</b>

3451
01:45:45,635 --> 01:45:47,570
<b>certainly many people would love to collaborate with them.</b>

3452
01:45:49,039 --> 01:45:49,839
<b>Is that so?</b>

3453
01:45:50,073 --> 01:45:51,207
<b>Ah, of course.</b>

3454
01:45:51,207 --> 01:45:52,609
<b>Right. I think</b>

3455
01:45:52,676 --> 01:45:55,812
<b>And look — all of it was serendipity.</b>

3456
01:45:55,979 --> 01:45:57,847
<b>With Kaiming it was just happening to be there</b>

3457
01:45:57,948 --> 01:46:00,383
<b>as an intern and getting him to open up.</b>

3458
01:46:00,383 --> 01:46:01,951
<b>And with Professor Fei-Fei,</b>

3459
01:46:01,951 --> 01:46:03,720
<b>you just had one meal together.</b>

3460
01:46:03,787 --> 01:46:05,722
<b>How did you get them to open up to you?</b>

3461
01:46:08,391 --> 01:46:10,760
<b>I think this is very hard to do intentionally.</b>

3462
01:46:11,328 --> 01:46:14,764
<b>Mm. Or this is a bit mysterious.</b>

3463
01:46:14,764 --> 01:46:18,335
<b>You could call it some kind of law of attraction.</b>

3464
01:46:18,335 --> 01:46:19,602
<b>Or you could think of it as</b>

3465
01:46:21,271 --> 01:46:23,006
<b>people whose thoughts align</b>

3466
01:46:23,006 --> 01:46:25,775
<b>ultimately converging together.</b>

3467
01:46:26,009 --> 01:46:27,344
<b>Though you may have countless small streams,</b>

3468
01:46:27,344 --> 01:46:30,213
<b>in the end, they may all converge into one river.</b>

3469
01:46:31,014 --> 01:46:32,415
<b>I think, for example,</b>

3470
01:46:32,782 --> 01:46:34,751
<b>uh, all the people I've mentioned,</b>

3471
01:46:34,751 --> 01:46:37,520
<b>at least they're all working on vision.</b>

3472
01:46:37,520 --> 01:46:38,555
<b>Or rather,</b>

3473
01:46:38,555 --> 01:46:39,389
<b>Even including Yann,</b>

3474
01:46:39,389 --> 01:46:41,324
<b>who can be seen as doing general AI,</b>

3475
01:46:41,324 --> 01:46:42,192
<b>but his starting point, right,</b>

3476
01:46:42,192 --> 01:46:43,827
<b>was also digit recognition,</b>

3477
01:46:43,827 --> 01:46:45,662
<b>which is also a visual problem.</b>

3478
01:46:46,196 --> 01:46:46,730
<b>Right.</b>

3479
01:46:46,730 --> 01:46:49,432
<b>I think everyone's foundation</b>

3480
01:46:49,432 --> 01:46:52,435
<b>is very, very aligned.</b>

3481
01:46:53,169 --> 01:46:54,537
<b>So I think</b>

3482
01:46:54,537 --> 01:46:57,240
<b>I really didn't make these things happen intentionally.</b>

3483
01:46:57,340 --> 01:46:57,741
<b>Right.</b>

3484
01:46:57,741 --> 01:46:58,341
<b>And many things,</b>

3485
01:46:58,341 --> 01:46:59,009
<b>Or rather, I think</b>

3486
01:46:59,009 --> 01:47:00,977
<b>don't need to be made to happen intentionally.</b>

3487
01:47:00,977 --> 01:47:04,414
<b>Everyone is just based on these research questions,</b>

3488
01:47:04,414 --> 01:47:06,516
<b>and their understanding of these questions,</b>

3489
01:47:06,516 --> 01:47:08,385
<b>collaborating together.</b>

3490
01:47:08,551 --> 01:47:09,786
<b>Right.</b>

3491
01:47:09,786 --> 01:47:10,820
<b>I would think of it this way.</b>

3492
01:47:10,820 --> 01:47:11,955
<b>The thing is that</b>

3493
01:47:11,955 --> 01:47:12,789
<b>from the outside,</b>

3494
01:47:12,789 --> 01:47:14,391
<b>I'd see you as someone very goal-oriented</b>

3495
01:47:14,391 --> 01:47:16,059
<b>and very logical.</b>

3496
01:47:16,159 --> 01:47:17,827
<b>But through our conversation just now,</b>

3497
01:47:17,827 --> 01:47:20,463
<b>I find you're someone whose choices are quite disorderly.</b>

3498
01:47:20,463 --> 01:47:21,264
<b>Right?</b>

3499
01:47:21,431 --> 01:47:21,798
<b>Right.</b>

3500
01:47:21,798 --> 01:47:24,067
<b>I think there's a certain disorder.</b>

3501
01:47:24,067 --> 01:47:24,567
<b>Mm. But I think</b>

3502
01:47:24,567 --> 01:47:26,770
<b>this is also a by-design process.</b>

3503
01:47:26,770 --> 01:47:29,272
<b>I choose this disorder.</b>

3504
01:47:29,272 --> 01:47:30,974
<b>I think</b>

3505
01:47:31,041 --> 01:47:31,474
<b>I think</b>

3506
01:47:31,474 --> 01:47:34,177
<b>Using this clichéd phrase:</b>

3507
01:47:34,177 --> 01:47:35,178
<b>"follow your heart."</b>

3508
01:47:35,178 --> 01:47:37,614
<b>Right. But in many cases</b>

3509
01:47:38,048 --> 01:47:39,749
<b>right, there's no way around it.</b>

3510
01:47:39,783 --> 01:47:42,585
<b>Many of my choices couldn't truly optimize</b>

3511
01:47:42,585 --> 01:47:44,454
<b>for a result.</b>

3512
01:47:44,454 --> 01:47:47,657
<b>I think this is the source of the disorder.</b>

3513
01:47:48,191 --> 01:47:49,159
<b>So in</b>

3514
01:47:49,159 --> 01:47:50,760
<b>these disorderly choices,</b>

3515
01:47:50,760 --> 01:47:53,329
<b>can you string together all of your research journey</b>

3516
01:47:53,329 --> 01:47:54,664
<b>into a single thread?</b>

3517
01:47:54,931 --> 01:47:56,933
<b>We've actually already discussed a few works.</b>

