<b>assuming this long river of history</b>

4691
02:23:01,435 --> 02:23:03,204
<b>means this curve continues forward,</b>

4692
02:23:03,204 --> 02:23:05,373
<b>right, there are times and times again</b>

4693
02:23:05,373 --> 02:23:06,541
<b>kind of</b>

4694
02:23:06,541 --> 02:23:07,241
<b>kind of</b>

4695
02:23:07,241 --> 02:23:07,742
<b>kind of</b>

4696
02:23:07,742 --> 02:23:10,077
<b>allowing everyone to break out of previous local optima</b>

4697
02:23:10,378 --> 02:23:12,747
<b>or enter the next stage —</b>

4698
02:23:12,747 --> 02:23:14,682
<b>such papers appear.</b>

4699
02:23:14,682 --> 02:23:17,084
<b>But I think we're still far from done.</b>

4700
02:23:17,084 --> 02:23:19,220
<b>This path is far from convergence.</b>

4701
02:23:19,287 --> 02:23:20,955
<b>I think there are still many things to be done.</b>

4702
02:23:20,955 --> 02:23:22,190
<b>I hope</b>

4703
02:23:22,390 --> 02:23:24,859
<b>I think it doesn't need to be me personally,</b>

4704
02:23:24,859 --> 02:23:25,293
<b>I hope</b>

4705
02:23:25,293 --> 02:23:27,828
<b>but at least I hope to be able to participate.</b>

4706
02:23:28,029 --> 02:23:29,096
<b>Right. I hope</b>

4707
02:23:29,096 --> 02:23:31,632
<b>assuming there's a next revolution,</b>

4708
02:23:31,799 --> 02:23:32,967
<b>I hope</b>

4709
02:23:32,967 --> 02:23:34,769
<b>I hope</b>

4710
02:23:34,769 --> 02:23:35,636
<b>looking back,</b>

4711
02:23:35,636 --> 02:23:36,604
<b>Right?</b>

4712
02:23:36,604 --> 02:23:38,873
<b>I said maybe it's not about creating some impact,</b>

4713
02:23:39,273 --> 02:23:41,943
<b>but because of my personal experience,</b>

4714
02:23:42,076 --> 02:23:44,946
<b>the patterns of collaboration around me,</b>

4715
02:23:44,946 --> 02:23:47,048
<b>my own understanding,</b>

4716
02:23:47,281 --> 02:23:48,549
<b>my own thinking,</b>

4717
02:23:49,584 --> 02:23:51,219
<b>I am able to understand certain things,</b>

4718
02:23:51,452 --> 02:23:54,355
<b>and what I understand can somehow</b>

4719
02:23:54,655 --> 02:23:57,658
<b>have some influence on</b>

4720
02:23:57,658 --> 02:24:00,394
<b>the world's or AI's development.</b>

4721
02:24:00,394 --> 02:24:00,795
<b>Mm.</b>

4722
02:24:00,795 --> 02:24:02,830
<b>I think</b>

4723
02:24:02,830 --> 02:24:05,132
<b>this is something I care very much about now.</b>

4724
02:24:05,132 --> 02:24:06,067
<b>Mm.</b>

4725
02:24:06,067 --> 02:24:08,469
<b>Is there no hope from LLMs for this?</b>

4726
02:24:09,070 --> 02:24:10,838
<b>The next revolution.</b>

4727
02:24:11,672 --> 02:24:12,740
<b>Again,</b>

4728
02:24:12,740 --> 02:24:14,775
<b>I think absolutely not.</b>

4729
02:24:14,942 --> 02:24:15,743
<b>No hope?</b>

4730
02:24:15,743 --> 02:24:16,277
<b>or</b>

4731
02:24:16,277 --> 02:24:20,014
<b>I would say LLMs will eventually fade.</b>

4732
02:24:20,014 --> 02:24:20,581
<b>No no no.</b>

4733
02:24:20,581 --> 02:24:21,382
<b>LLMs</b>

4734
02:24:21,882 --> 02:24:23,751
<b>will never die,</b>

4735
02:24:23,751 --> 02:24:25,286
<b>but will eventually fade.</b>

4736
02:24:25,286 --> 02:24:26,220
<b>Old soldiers never die,</b>

4737
02:24:26,220 --> 02:24:27,021
<b>they just fade away.</b>

4738
02:24:27,021 --> 02:24:28,089
<b>Right?</b>

4739
02:24:28,089 --> 02:24:29,457
<b>Why will they eventually fade?</b>

4740
02:24:30,224 --> 02:24:30,992
<b>They won't die.</b>

4741
02:24:30,992 --> 02:24:32,026
<b>They will just fade away.</b>

4742
02:24:32,026 --> 02:24:34,695
<b>That is, it will definitely have its value,</b>

4743
02:24:34,829 --> 02:24:35,963
<b>it's a very good tool.</b>

4744
02:24:35,963 --> 02:24:37,431
<b>I use LLMs every day now.</b>

4745
02:24:37,732 --> 02:24:40,801
<b>But it's not the foundation for building a universal,</b>

4746
02:24:40,801 --> 02:24:43,237
<b>a general intelligence system.</b>

4747
02:24:43,237 --> 02:24:45,573
<b>It's not the world model's</b>

4748
02:24:45,706 --> 02:24:47,041
<b>kind of</b>

4749
02:24:47,041 --> 02:24:49,243
<b>foundation of this building.</b>

4750
02:24:49,243 --> 02:24:49,844
<b>World model,</b>

4751
02:24:49,844 --> 02:24:50,811
<b>we'll talk about it later.</b>

4752
02:24:50,811 --> 02:24:51,379
<b>Your work —</b>

4753
02:24:51,379 --> 02:24:52,413
<b>do you want to expand on it?</b>

4754
02:24:52,413 --> 02:24:52,847
<b>You've already</b>

4755
02:24:52,847 --> 02:24:53,547
<b>let me say a bit more.</b>

4756
02:24:53,547 --> 02:24:54,282
<b>Is there time?</b>

4757
02:24:54,282 --> 02:24:57,551
<b>Yes. You've already said you haven't reached Max.</b>

4758
02:24:57,551 --> 02:24:58,986
<b>Yes, yes, right.</b>

4759
02:24:58,986 --> 02:25:00,288
<b>Put that way,</b>

4760
02:25:00,288 --> 02:25:02,189
<b>it seems there's nothing much to talk about with these works.</b>

4761
02:25:02,189 --> 02:25:03,424
<b>But I think there's still some significance.</b>

4762
02:25:03,424 --> 02:25:04,091
<b>Because</b>

4763
02:25:04,091 --> 02:25:06,494
<b>Just like I said about non-linear research,</b>

4764
02:25:06,661 --> 02:25:08,462
<b>right, in a paper,</b>

4765
02:25:08,462 --> 02:25:09,830
<b>we first do some things,</b>

4766
02:25:09,830 --> 02:25:10,965
<b>then gradually</b>

4767
02:25:11,065 --> 02:25:12,667
<b>build up some reserves,</b>

4768
02:25:12,667 --> 02:25:14,001
<b>and then in the last month,</b>

4769
02:25:14,001 --> 02:25:15,336
<b>find a new direction,</b>

4770
02:25:15,336 --> 02:25:16,270
<b>deliver</b>

4771
02:25:16,270 --> 02:25:17,138
<b>the final result.</b>

4772
02:25:17,138 --> 02:25:18,139
<b>Mm. I think,</b>

4773
02:25:18,239 --> 02:25:20,641
<b>When I look at all my previous work,</b>

4774
02:25:20,808 --> 02:25:22,743
<b>I also have this feeling:</b>

4775
02:25:22,810 --> 02:25:26,681
<b>I'm still in that initial confused exploration phase.</b>

4776
02:25:27,148 --> 02:25:27,782
<b>But who knows —</b>

4777
02:25:27,782 --> 02:25:28,449
<b>maybe this year,</b>

4778
02:25:28,449 --> 02:25:29,383
<b>maybe next year,</b>

4779
02:25:29,450 --> 02:25:30,885
<b>maybe</b>

4780
02:25:30,885 --> 02:25:32,219
<b>I suddenly</b>

4781
02:25:32,219 --> 02:25:33,454
<b>right, have a spiritual awakening,</b>

4782
02:25:33,621 --> 02:25:35,489
<b>and can produce some more meaningful work.</b>

4783
02:25:35,489 --> 02:25:36,257
<b>Mm-hmm.</b>

4784
02:25:36,257 --> 02:25:38,025
<b>But I think the foundation here is</b>

4785
02:25:38,225 --> 02:25:39,694
<b>as I just said,</b>

4786
02:25:39,694 --> 02:25:41,595
<b>it needs to be able to string together a thread.</b>

4787
02:25:41,829 --> 02:25:42,596
<b>Or rather,</b>

4788
02:25:42,596 --> 02:25:43,531
<b>it's actually not a line,</b>

4789
02:25:43,531 --> 02:25:44,732
<b>it's a graph.</b>

4790
02:25:45,032 --> 02:25:46,634
<b>It has different nodes,</b>

4791
02:25:46,634 --> 02:25:48,035
<b>different nodes connected to each other,</b>

4792
02:25:48,035 --> 02:25:49,470
<b>each node is a paper,</b>

4793
02:25:49,603 --> 02:25:51,472
<b>all with connections between them.</b>

4794
02:25:51,939 --> 02:25:53,240
<b>Your subsequent papers</b>

4795
02:25:53,474 --> 02:25:56,010
<b>are all influenced by all the previous papers.</b>

4796
02:25:56,010 --> 02:25:57,011
<b>Mm, right.</b>

4797
02:25:57,178 --> 02:25:58,345
<b>So later,</b>

4798
02:25:58,345 --> 02:25:59,947
<b>for example, Contrastive Learning,</b>

4799
02:25:59,947 --> 02:26:00,548
<b>making it work means</b>

4800
02:26:00,548 --> 02:26:03,217
<b>we saw for the first time in visual tasks</b>

4801
02:26:03,617 --> 02:26:05,252
<b>MoCo</b>

4802
02:26:05,252 --> 02:26:05,986
<b>such work,</b>

4803
02:26:05,986 --> 02:26:06,754
<b>especially we had</b>

4804
02:26:06,754 --> 02:26:07,388
<b>V1, V2,</b>

4805
02:26:07,388 --> 02:26:08,189
<b>V3, right?</b>

4806
02:26:08,189 --> 02:26:09,223
<b>And in V3,</b>

4807
02:26:09,223 --> 02:26:10,091
<b>we used Transformer,</b>

4808
02:26:10,858 --> 02:26:11,959
<b>and we scaled up,</b>

4809
02:26:12,293 --> 02:26:12,893
<b>Uh,</b>

4810
02:26:12,893 --> 02:26:15,696
<b>actually already better than the representation ImageNet could get,</b>

4811
02:26:15,696 --> 02:26:18,499
<b>across all kinds of tasks.</b>

4812
02:26:18,499 --> 02:26:20,568
<b>This for us was</b>

4813
02:26:20,568 --> 02:26:22,470
<b>actually a major surprise.</b>

4814
02:26:22,470 --> 02:26:23,337
<b>Mm.</b>

4815
02:26:23,437 --> 02:26:24,238
<b>Mm-hmm.</b>

4816
02:26:24,238 --> 02:26:25,573
<b>At that time,</b>

4817
02:26:25,573 --> 02:26:26,841
<b>at that point,</b>

4818
02:26:27,041 --> 02:26:28,676
<b>I thought, wow,</b>

4819
02:26:28,676 --> 02:26:31,412
<b>everything is flourishing again.</b>

4820
02:26:31,412 --> 02:26:34,415
<b>Our problem can basically be answered.</b>

4821
02:26:34,749 --> 02:26:36,183
<b>We found a way —</b>

4822
02:26:36,183 --> 02:26:36,884
<b>self-supervised learning —</b>

4823
02:26:36,884 --> 02:26:37,752
<b>that can work.</b>

4824
02:26:37,952 --> 02:26:38,285
<b>Going forward,</b>

4825
02:26:38,285 --> 02:26:40,621
<b>we just need to scale up what we're doing now,</b>

4826
02:26:40,788 --> 02:26:41,222
<b>and</b>

4827
02:26:41,222 --> 02:26:42,857
<b>the future is incredibly bright.</b>

4828
02:26:42,857 --> 02:26:43,891
<b>But unfortunately,</b>

4829
02:26:43,891 --> 02:26:44,959
<b>this also didn't happen.</b>

4830
02:26:44,959 --> 02:26:45,960
<b>Right?</b>

4831
02:26:45,993 --> 02:26:47,027
<b>But before that,</b>

4832
02:26:47,027 --> 02:26:47,962
<b>we had another paper,</b>

4833
02:26:47,962 --> 02:26:48,863
<b>also</b>

4834
02:26:48,863 --> 02:26:51,966
<b>MoCo and MAE by the way were both projects Kaiming led.</b>

4835
02:26:52,166 --> 02:26:54,235
<b>Actually, people say</b>

4836
02:26:54,235 --> 02:26:55,469
<b>what does it mean to lead a project?</b>

4837
02:26:55,469 --> 02:26:56,937
<b>I think</b>

4838
02:26:56,937 --> 02:26:59,039
<b>Kaiming truly demonstrated this leadership —</b>

4839
02:26:59,039 --> 02:26:59,840
<b>that is,</b>

4840
02:26:59,840 --> 02:27:04,412
<b>he truly took on 80-90% of the first-author</b>

4841
02:27:04,412 --> 02:27:05,613
<b>plus last-author</b>

4842
02:27:05,613 --> 02:27:07,081
<b>or corresponding-author responsibilities.</b>

4843
02:27:07,081 --> 02:27:08,883
<b>The corresponding author's responsibilities.</b>

4844
02:27:09,083 --> 02:27:12,052
<b>He needed to write the baseline himself,</b>

4845
02:27:12,086 --> 02:27:14,422
<b>run many, many experiments himself,</b>

4846
02:27:14,555 --> 02:27:16,490
<b>finalize the paper himself,</b>

4847
02:27:16,490 --> 02:27:18,092
<b>tell the story, present it,</b>

4848
02:27:18,092 --> 02:27:20,027
<b>all of these things</b>

4849
02:27:20,027 --> 02:27:22,863
<b>basically Kaiming did single-handedly.</b>

4850
02:27:22,963 --> 02:27:23,798
<b>And accomplished it.</b>

4851
02:27:23,798 --> 02:27:25,032
<b>So what about others?</b>

4852
02:27:25,032 --> 02:27:26,133
<b>Others,</b>

4853
02:27:26,167 --> 02:27:27,134
<b>we</b>

4854
02:27:27,134 --> 02:27:28,536
<b>of course also participated</b>

4855
02:27:28,536 --> 02:27:29,370
<b>and made contributions.</b>

4856
02:27:29,370 --> 02:27:30,137
<b>But I'm just saying</b>

4857
02:27:30,137 --> 02:27:32,339
<b>this is a path Kaiming led.</b>

4858
02:27:32,406 --> 02:27:34,275
<b>Right, we</b>

4859
02:27:34,742 --> 02:27:38,546
<b>accelerated the progress of this,</b>

4860
02:27:38,546 --> 02:27:40,214
<b>and may have made the results much better too.</b>

4861
02:27:40,214 --> 02:27:40,881
<b>Mm.</b>

4862
02:27:40,881 --> 02:27:42,683
<b>But it doesn't change the essence of this.</b>

4863
02:27:42,983 --> 02:27:44,285
<b>Right.</b>

4864
02:27:44,285 --> 02:27:45,586
<b>So this is Kaiming.</b>

4865
02:27:45,586 --> 02:27:48,155
<b>Even now, for example, just a couple days ago he told me</b>

4866
02:27:48,255 --> 02:27:49,690
<b>he really enjoys this kind of</b>

4867
02:27:49,690 --> 02:27:51,492
<b>IC work — individual contributor,</b>

4868
02:27:51,492 --> 02:27:53,160
<b>the individual contributor</b>

4869
02:27:53,160 --> 02:27:54,695
<b>type of role.</b>

4870
02:27:54,695 --> 02:27:55,262
<b>Mm.</b>

4871
02:27:55,262 --> 02:27:58,165
<b>He doesn't enjoy managing a large team,</b>

4872
02:27:58,165 --> 02:27:58,999
<b>getting everyone together,</b>

4873
02:27:58,999 --> 02:28:01,335
<b>just being a manager pointing the direction.</b>

4874
02:28:01,335 --> 02:28:02,636
<b>He doesn't like that.</b>

4875
02:28:02,636 --> 02:28:03,838
<b>How many people does he manage now?</b>

4876
02:28:03,838 --> 02:28:04,839
<b>He has many, many people.</b>

4877
02:28:04,839 --> 02:28:06,640
<b>He now has many undergraduates</b>

4878
02:28:06,640 --> 02:28:07,475
<b>visiting him,</b>

4879
02:28:07,641 --> 02:28:09,543
<b>and he</b>

4880
02:28:09,543 --> 02:28:11,412
<b>is also doing a lot of really great work.</b>

4881
02:28:11,412 --> 02:28:12,646
<b>So I actually don't believe him.</b>

4882
02:28:12,646 --> 02:28:13,480
<b>I tell him,</b>

4883
02:28:13,480 --> 02:28:15,649
<b>"You're actually a very good manager."</b>

4884
02:28:15,649 --> 02:28:17,184
<b>At least for me,</b>

4885
02:28:17,184 --> 02:28:18,652
<b>even though you never really managed me,</b>

4886
02:28:18,652 --> 02:28:21,689
<b>just being around you,</b>

4887
02:28:21,689 --> 02:28:25,826
<b>I could feel my own efficiency improving,</b>

4888
02:28:25,826 --> 02:28:27,862
<b>feeling like I was getting smarter.</b>

4889
02:28:27,962 --> 02:28:28,496
<b>I think</b>

4890
02:28:28,496 --> 02:28:30,531
<b>If I were going to have a manager,</b>

4891
02:28:30,531 --> 02:28:32,967
<b>I'd want one like that —</b>

4892
02:28:32,967 --> 02:28:37,238
<b>Right?</b>
<b>one who can empower the people around him to get better.</b>

4893
02:28:37,438 --> 02:28:38,072
<b>Right.</b>

4894
02:28:38,072 --> 02:28:39,073
<b>I think this is Kaiming.</b>

4895
02:28:39,073 --> 02:28:40,341
<b>So MAE —</b>

4896
02:28:40,341 --> 02:28:41,275
<b>in any case,</b>

4897
02:28:41,408 --> 02:28:43,644
<b>we explored the Contrastive Learning path,</b>

4898
02:28:43,644 --> 02:28:44,545
<b>and found</b>

4899
02:28:44,545 --> 02:28:46,046
<b>it couldn't scale up.</b>

4900
02:28:46,046 --> 02:28:47,481
<b>So we wanted to switch directions.</b>

4901
02:28:47,681 --> 02:28:49,083
<b>So we went back</b>

4902
02:28:49,083 --> 02:28:50,417
<b>and used a simpler approach,</b>

4903
02:28:50,417 --> 02:28:52,486
<b>which is a kind of denoising</b>

4904
02:28:52,486 --> 02:28:53,354
<b>autoencoder,</b>

4905
02:28:53,354 --> 02:28:55,055
<b>this kind of autoencoder,</b>

4906
02:28:55,055 --> 02:28:57,892
<b>the Masked Autoencoder (MAE).</b>

4907
02:28:57,892 --> 02:28:59,026
<b>This method is even simpler.</b>

4908
02:28:59,026 --> 02:29:01,195
<b>Everyone can go read the paper,</b>

4909
02:29:01,395 --> 02:29:02,897
<b>But in short,</b>

4910
02:29:02,897 --> 02:29:04,598
<b>but basically by taking some images</b>

4911
02:29:04,598 --> 02:29:06,000
<b>and corrupting them,</b>

4912
02:29:06,000 --> 02:29:08,469
<b>then reconstructing</b>

4913
02:29:08,469 --> 02:29:09,436
<b>these</b>

4914
02:29:09,436 --> 02:29:10,571
<b>noisy images,</b>

4915
02:29:10,571 --> 02:29:11,539
<b>cropped images,</b>

4916
02:29:11,539 --> 02:29:13,340
<b>or masked images,</b>

4917
02:29:13,340 --> 02:29:13,974
<b>to learn representations.</b>

4918
02:29:13,974 --> 02:29:14,408
<b>Mm.</b>

4919
02:29:14,408 --> 02:29:15,009
<b>This</b>

4920
02:29:15,009 --> 02:29:17,778
<b>fundamentally different from Contrastive Learning,</b>

4921
02:29:17,878 --> 02:29:19,747
<b>but its results were also very good,</b>

4922
02:29:19,747 --> 02:29:21,749
<b>although it has very different characteristics.</b>

4923
02:29:21,815 --> 02:29:23,951
<b>For example, it doesn't explicitly</b>

4924
02:29:23,951 --> 02:29:25,486
<b>model certain environments</b>

4925
02:29:25,486 --> 02:29:26,954
<b>this kind of invariance</b>

4926
02:29:27,021 --> 02:29:29,490
