9009
04:35:27,707 --> 04:35:29,409
<b>even though it has no actions</b>

9010
04:35:29,409 --> 04:35:31,578
<b>it has no real understanding of the physical world</b>

9011
04:35:31,678 --> 04:35:34,280
<b>and it can't truly reason and plan</b>

9012
04:35:34,280 --> 04:35:36,616
<b>because its planning through CoT</b>

9013
04:35:36,616 --> 04:35:38,485
<b>and its reasoning through CoT</b>

9014
04:35:38,485 --> 04:35:39,252
<b>is still very different</b>

9015
04:35:39,252 --> 04:35:40,053
<b>from what I just described</b>

9016
04:35:40,053 --> 04:35:41,521
<b>like MPC-level</b>

9017
04:35:41,521 --> 04:35:43,056
<b>planning</b>

9018
04:35:43,056 --> 04:35:44,324
<b>CoT also brings its own set of problems</b>

9019
04:35:44,324 --> 04:35:45,291
<b>but all that's fine</b>

9020
04:35:45,859 --> 04:35:47,127
<b>but the next step</b>

9021
04:35:47,127 --> 04:35:47,660
<b>you'll see</b>

9022
04:35:47,660 --> 04:35:51,731
<b>for example everyone's doing</b>

9023
04:35:51,931 --> 04:35:52,799
<b>whether DiT or</b>

9024
04:35:52,799 --> 04:35:54,033
<b>whatever model</b>

9025
04:35:54,033 --> 04:35:57,270
<b>but people started doing generative models</b>

9026
04:35:57,270 --> 04:36:00,874
<b>and that has made things somewhat different</b>

9027
04:36:00,874 --> 04:36:01,241
<b>right?</b>

9028
04:36:01,241 --> 04:36:02,509
<b>mm-hmm, and that's why many people</b>

9029
04:36:02,509 --> 04:36:04,444
<b>who do video generation call it a world model</b>

9030
04:36:04,444 --> 04:36:06,446
<b>I think that's understandable</b>

9031
04:36:06,446 --> 04:36:06,846
<b>although</b>

9032
04:36:06,846 --> 04:36:09,716
<b>I don't agree that the video generation</b>

9033
04:36:09,716 --> 04:36:10,617
<b>model they're doing</b>

9034
04:36:10,617 --> 04:36:13,686
<b>is the final end game world model</b>

9035
04:36:13,686 --> 04:36:17,056
<b>but it has indeed pushed one step beyond language models</b>

9036
04:36:17,724 --> 04:36:19,058
<b>right</b>

9037
04:36:19,058 --> 04:36:20,460
<b>how does it do that?</b>

9038
04:36:20,460 --> 04:36:22,829
<b>on top of language models</b>

9039
04:36:23,129 --> 04:36:23,730
<b>uh</b>

9040
04:36:23,730 --> 04:36:25,798
<b>I think all these systems now</b>

9041
04:36:25,798 --> 04:36:28,468
<b>actually still rely on language models</b>

9042
04:36:28,635 --> 04:36:29,068
<b>right?</b>

9043
04:36:29,068 --> 04:36:32,238
<b>they still use language models to do prompt</b>

9044
04:36:32,238 --> 04:36:34,374
<b>rewriting and then to help</b>

9045
04:36:34,407 --> 04:36:36,242
<b>serve as a conditioning</b>

9046
04:36:36,442 --> 04:36:38,912
<b>fed into the video generation model</b>

9047
04:36:38,912 --> 04:36:41,881
<b>and language models have actually become</b>

9048
04:36:41,881 --> 04:36:43,183
<b>you know</b>

9049
04:36:43,183 --> 04:36:44,517
<b>the historical progression here is quite interesting</b>

9050
04:36:44,517 --> 04:36:45,985
<b>language models used to be the main thing</b>

9051
04:36:46,152 --> 04:36:47,820
<b>now language models have become</b>

9052
04:36:47,820 --> 04:36:51,090
<b>a preparatory step for video generation models</b>

9053
04:36:51,090 --> 04:36:52,258
<b>a scaffolding</b>

9054
04:36:52,659 --> 04:36:54,694
<b>in the old language models</b>

9055
04:36:54,694 --> 04:36:56,062
<b>what you modeled was P(y)</b>

9056
04:36:56,062 --> 04:36:59,165
<b>right?</b>
<b>and that y is still in some semantic space</b>

9057
04:36:59,165 --> 04:37:00,867
<b>information in some kind of label space</b>

9058
04:37:00,867 --> 04:37:03,269
<b>mm-hmm, but now with video generation models</b>

9059
04:37:03,269 --> 04:37:06,206
<b>what you model is the probability P(x|y)</b>

9060
04:37:06,839 --> 04:37:07,874
<b>what this means is</b>

9061
04:37:07,974 --> 04:37:10,176
<b>what you're modeling now is already x</b>

9062
04:37:10,176 --> 04:37:12,045
<b>x is the data itself</b>

9063
04:37:12,211 --> 04:37:13,513
<b>your y has become</b>

9064
04:37:13,513 --> 04:37:16,249
<b>a condition — this is already very different</b>

9065
04:37:16,249 --> 04:37:16,883
<b>okay</b>

9066
04:37:16,883 --> 04:37:17,684
<b>why is it so different?</b>

9067
04:37:17,684 --> 04:37:21,187
<b>it's because when you have a low dimensional y</b>

9068
04:37:21,187 --> 04:37:21,888
<b>space</b>

9069
04:37:21,888 --> 04:37:22,589
<b>and then you</b>

9070
04:37:22,589 --> 04:37:26,392
<b>go to model such a distribution</b>

9071
04:37:26,392 --> 04:37:27,594
<b>your probability density</b>

9072
04:37:27,594 --> 04:37:29,696
<b>only competes within your y's distribution</b>

9073
04:37:29,729 --> 04:37:31,531
<b>meaning</b>

9074
04:37:31,531 --> 04:37:32,899
<b>the likelihood you assign</b>

9075
04:37:32,899 --> 04:37:34,634
<b>I'm getting a bit too technical here</b>

9076
04:37:34,634 --> 04:37:35,835
<b>but anyway</b>

9077
04:37:35,835 --> 04:37:37,470
<b>or let's not talk about language models first</b>

9078
04:37:37,470 --> 04:37:37,971
<b>let's first talk about</b>

9079
04:37:37,971 --> 04:37:38,771
<b>say</b>

9080
04:37:38,805 --> 04:37:41,608
<b>a model that classifies 1000 categories</b>

9081
04:37:41,608 --> 04:37:41,975
<b>you can think of</b>

9082
04:37:41,975 --> 04:37:44,177
<b>these few labels as a precursor to language</b>

9083
04:37:44,310 --> 04:37:47,380
<b>it's also a low-dimensional vocabulary</b>

9084
04:37:47,380 --> 04:37:48,181
<b>right?</b>

9085
04:37:48,214 --> 04:37:50,450
<b>and then</b>
<b>if you're doing a classification problem like this</b>

9086
04:37:50,650 --> 04:37:53,820
<b>all the decisions you need to make are</b>

9087
04:37:53,920 --> 04:37:55,822
<b>if this thing is a cat</b>

9088
04:37:55,822 --> 04:37:57,056
<b>it can't be a dog</b>

9089
04:37:57,323 --> 04:37:57,890
<b>right?</b>

9090
04:37:57,890 --> 04:38:00,326
<b>this thing is constrained by my label set</b>

9091
04:38:00,326 --> 04:38:01,127
<b>mm-hmm</b>

9092
04:38:01,828 --> 04:38:04,831
<b>but when you start modeling P(x|y)</b>

9093
04:38:04,831 --> 04:38:06,432
<b>when you're doing a generative model</b>

9094
04:38:06,499 --> 04:38:10,403
<b>the likelihood you assign in this case says</b>

9095
04:38:10,403 --> 04:38:12,905
<b>what phenomena actually exist in the world</b>

9096
04:38:13,039 --> 04:38:15,174
<b>which things are more likely to exist</b>

9097
04:38:15,808 --> 04:38:17,577
<b>that becomes very very different</b>

9098
04:38:17,577 --> 04:38:19,779
<b>right? because what you need to learn now</b>

9099
04:38:19,779 --> 04:38:21,581
<b>the amount of intelligence information</b>

9100
04:38:21,581 --> 04:38:23,883
<b>is far greater than what you get from modeling P(Y)</b>

9101
04:38:24,317 --> 04:38:27,320
