12122
06:10:08,015 --> 06:10:09,250
<b>very much like House of Cards</b>

12123
06:10:09,250 --> 06:10:11,085
<b>or how there's a lot of scheming</b>

12124
06:10:11,085 --> 06:10:13,220
<b>how you form alliances</b>

12125
06:10:13,220 --> 06:10:16,524
<b>then maneuver and rise to the top</b>

12126
06:10:16,524 --> 06:10:18,826
<b>and so on</b>

12127
06:10:18,826 --> 06:10:21,128
<b>I think that's very interesting</b>

12128
06:10:21,228 --> 06:10:23,130
<b>[laughter]</b>
<b>and one thing that left a deep impression on me</b>

12129
06:10:23,130 --> 06:10:24,498
<b>was that</b>

12130
06:10:24,565 --> 06:10:25,299
<b>for example, they</b>

12131
06:10:25,299 --> 06:10:26,233
<b>these animals actually</b>

12132
06:10:26,233 --> 06:10:29,003
<b>including chimpanzees, also have a kind of theory of mind</b>

12133
06:10:29,003 --> 06:10:30,771
<b>they can also have their own world model</b>

12134
06:10:30,771 --> 06:10:32,406
<b>and their world models are actually quite good</b>

12135
06:10:32,473 --> 06:10:34,041
<b>for example, there's an example where</b>

12136
06:10:34,041 --> 06:10:36,177
<b>an experimenter is in a room</b>

12137
06:10:36,177 --> 06:10:38,312
<b>with two boxes</b>

12138
06:10:38,312 --> 06:10:41,515
<b>one box containing a banana</b>

12139
06:10:41,515 --> 06:10:42,616
<b>the other containing an apple</b>

12140
06:10:42,650 --> 06:10:44,785
<b>the chimp is shown this</b>

12141
06:10:44,785 --> 06:10:46,520
<b>then the boxes are closed</b>

12142
06:10:46,620 --> 06:10:48,222
<b>[laughter]</b>

12143
06:10:48,222 --> 06:10:50,057
<b>and the experimenter takes the chimp out</b>

12144
06:10:50,057 --> 06:10:51,425
<b>after a long, long time</b>

12145
06:10:51,425 --> 06:10:53,727
<b>it's brought back into the room</b>

12146
06:10:53,794 --> 06:10:56,397
<b>and the first thing the chimp notices</b>

12147
06:10:56,597 --> 06:10:58,599
<b>is that</b>

12148
06:10:58,599 --> 06:11:02,369
<b>the experimenter is eating a banana</b>

12149
06:11:02,436 --> 06:11:03,170
<b>and the chimp</b>

12150
06:11:03,170 --> 06:11:03,604
<b>immediately</b>

12151
06:11:03,604 --> 06:11:06,373
<b>goes straight to open the box with the apple</b>

12152
06:11:06,373 --> 06:11:07,441
<b>and eats the apple</b>

12153
06:11:07,908 --> 06:11:09,410
<b>without even glancing at the banana</b>

12154
06:11:10,044 --> 06:11:10,845
<b>so</b>

12155
06:11:10,845 --> 06:11:15,049
<b>chimpanzees also have a kind of reasoning ability</b>

12156
06:11:15,115 --> 06:11:15,416
<b>right?</b>

12157
06:11:15,416 --> 06:11:17,918
<b>and although language is indeed unique</b>

12158
06:11:17,918 --> 06:11:20,854
<b>language is something only humans have</b>

12159
06:11:20,854 --> 06:11:23,457
<b>but that doesn't mean other animals don't communicate</b>

12160
06:11:23,624 --> 06:11:24,191
<b>if we</b>

12161
06:11:24,191 --> 06:11:25,092
<b>they have their own language</b>

12162
06:11:25,092 --> 06:11:26,093
<b>they have their own language</b>

12163
06:11:26,093 --> 06:11:26,493
<b>including</b>

12164
06:11:26,493 --> 06:11:29,663
<b>like whales also have their own language</b>

12165
06:11:29,797 --> 06:11:31,298
<b>anyway this is all quite fascinating</b>

12166
06:11:31,298 --> 06:11:32,633
<b>I highly recommend that book</b>

12167
06:11:32,633 --> 06:11:33,267
<b>[laughter]</b>

12168
06:11:33,267 --> 06:11:33,868
<b>and there's also</b>

12169
06:11:33,868 --> 06:11:35,869
<b>I read about some kind of bird (scrub jays)</b>

12170
06:11:35,869 --> 06:11:37,204
<b>I forgot what they're called</b>

12171
06:11:37,238 --> 06:11:39,006
<b>apparently they're very good at</b>

12172
06:11:39,006 --> 06:11:41,408
<b>if one is burying food</b>

12173
06:11:41,408 --> 06:11:43,811
<b>burying food underground</b>

12174
06:11:43,844 --> 06:11:44,879
<b>if it notices</b>

12175
06:11:44,879 --> 06:11:47,181
<b>that one of its peers saw it happen</b>

12176
06:11:47,514 --> 06:11:48,883
<b>it will first bury it there</b>

12177
06:11:48,883 --> 06:11:51,418
<b>then wait for the peer to leave, dig it up</b>

12178
06:11:51,418 --> 06:11:52,987
<b>and rebury it in a different spot</b>

12179
06:11:54,255 --> 06:11:56,290
<b>I think that's quite interesting</b>

12180
06:11:56,290 --> 06:11:57,825
<b>and of course we also know</b>

12181
06:11:57,825 --> 06:11:59,226
<b>dogs have a keen sense of smell</b>

12182
06:11:59,226 --> 06:12:01,662
<b>and bats navigate by hearing</b>

12183
06:12:01,829 --> 06:12:05,633
<b>I think the boundaries of intelligence are very broad</b>

12184
06:12:05,799 --> 06:12:09,036
<b>people now talk about jagged intelligence</b>

12185
06:12:09,036 --> 06:12:10,471
<b>so your world model</b>

12186
06:12:10,471 --> 06:12:14,808
<b>which type of biological intelligence will it aim for first?</b>

12187
06:12:14,908 --> 06:12:16,210
<b>the goal is of course human intelligence</b>

12188
06:12:16,210 --> 06:12:18,212
<b>human intelligence is certainly</b>

12189
06:12:18,212 --> 06:12:19,513
<b>still</b>

12190
06:12:19,513 --> 06:12:21,582
<b>at least in one dimension still the strongest</b>

12191
06:12:21,582 --> 06:12:21,916
<b>or</b>

12192
06:12:21,916 --> 06:12:24,852
<b>it's also what can most benefit the world</b>

12193
06:12:24,852 --> 06:12:25,386
<b>Mm-hmm</b>

12194
06:12:25,386 --> 06:12:27,721
<b>so we still want to build a world model</b>

12195
06:12:27,721 --> 06:12:29,890
<b>toward human-like intelligence</b>

12196
06:12:29,923 --> 06:12:30,457
<b>Mm-hmm</b>

12197
06:12:30,457 --> 06:12:33,127
<b>but I just want to let go of human arrogance</b>

12198
06:12:33,394 --> 06:12:35,629
<b>and recently I've been very inspired by this</b>

12199
06:12:35,629 --> 06:12:37,665
<b>because I watched Rich Sutton</b>

12200
06:12:37,665 --> 06:12:39,366
<b>in this</b>

12201
06:12:39,366 --> 06:12:41,035
<b>podcast</b>

12202
06:12:41,035 --> 06:12:41,835
<b>talk about a theory</b>

12203
06:12:41,835 --> 06:12:42,670
<b>because before I</b>

12204
06:12:42,670 --> 06:12:44,605
<b>didn't know how to address this</b>

12205
06:12:44,872 --> 06:12:46,206
<b>because people say</b>

12206
06:12:46,307 --> 06:12:47,675
<b>LLMs are amazing, right?</b>

12207
06:12:47,775 --> 06:12:49,276
<b>LLMs can now write code</b>

12208
06:12:49,376 --> 06:12:51,879
<b>can win gold at the IMO and IOI</b>

12209
06:12:52,079 --> 06:12:54,682
<b>can help us go to the moon and Mars</b>

12210
06:12:54,982 --> 06:12:56,317
<b>these things are incredible</b>

12211
06:12:57,217 --> 06:12:59,453
<b>and I can't deny these things</b>

12212
06:12:59,453 --> 06:13:00,688
<b>they really are impressive</b>

12213
06:13:00,888 --> 06:13:01,689
<b>right?</b>

12214
06:13:01,689 --> 06:13:04,825
<b>but Rich Sutton's reply</b>

12215
06:13:04,825 --> 06:13:05,192
<b>I think</b>

12216
06:13:05,192 --> 06:13:06,994
<b>was very good — he replied</b>

12217
06:13:07,194 --> 06:13:09,129
<b>you think these things are great and impressive?</b>

12218
06:13:09,129 --> 06:13:11,265
<b>that they're hard? well, feel free to think that</b>

12219
06:13:11,265 --> 06:13:12,499
<b>because I don't think so</b>

12220
06:13:13,000 --> 06:13:16,570
<b>I think building the intelligence of a squirrel</b>

12221
06:13:17,104 --> 06:13:18,906
<b>is the hard problem</b>

12222
06:13:19,573 --> 06:13:21,375
<b>once you have a squirrel's intelligence</b>

12223
06:13:21,775 --> 06:13:24,011
<b>once you can build a squirrel's intelligence</b>

12224
06:13:24,011 --> 06:13:26,714
<b>and make it survive in the real world</b>

12225
06:13:26,780 --> 06:13:27,815
<b>with its own goals</b>

12226
06:13:27,815 --> 06:13:29,016
<b>its own objectives</b>

12227
06:13:29,016 --> 06:13:31,618
<b>its own intrinsic rewards as you described</b>

12228
06:13:31,919 --> 06:13:32,920
<b>it knows hunger</b>

12229
06:13:32,920 --> 06:13:34,221
<b>it has its own emotions</b>

12230
06:13:35,022 --> 06:13:37,124
<b>and it can engage in social activities</b>

12231
06:13:37,925 --> 06:13:42,262
<b>after that, writing code, going to Mars, going to the moon</b>

12232
06:13:42,262 --> 06:13:44,365
<b>those things would be the easy ones</b>

12233
06:13:45,265 --> 06:13:45,866
<b>Good</b>

12234
06:13:45,866 --> 06:13:48,168
<b>I'm gradually coming to strongly agree with this view</b>

12235
06:13:48,435 --> 06:13:50,237
<b>if you set aside human arrogance</b>

12236
06:13:50,237 --> 06:13:52,706
<b>building a squirrel's intelligence</b>

12237
06:13:52,706 --> 06:13:54,375
<b>is actually a harder problem</b>

12238
06:13:54,641 --> 06:13:56,210
<b>but that's not how it looks to humans</b>

12239
06:13:56,477 --> 06:13:57,578
<b>from a human's</b>

12240
06:13:57,578 --> 06:13:59,513
<b>perspective</b>

12241
06:13:59,513 --> 06:14:00,180
<b>it doesn't seem that way</b>

12242
06:14:00,180 --> 06:14:02,249
<b>but that's entirely due to human arrogance</b>

12243
06:14:03,083 --> 06:14:05,419
<b>you're also building human-level intelligence</b>

12244
06:14:05,586 --> 06:14:06,320
<b>ah, yes</b>

12245
06:14:06,320 --> 06:14:07,021
<b>but what I mean is</b>

12246
06:14:07,021 --> 06:14:09,723
<b>human intelligence has many, many aspects</b>

12247
06:14:09,723 --> 06:14:12,793
<b>human intelligence is not just a language model</b>

12248
06:14:12,793 --> 06:14:14,928
<b>human intelligence encompasses many types of intelligence</b>

12249
06:14:14,928 --> 06:14:16,663
<b>that cannot be defined</b>

12250
06:14:16,663 --> 06:14:19,032
<b>by language models or language itself</b>

12251
06:14:19,600 --> 06:14:22,202
<b>right, I think that's a core insight</b>

12252
06:14:22,202 --> 06:14:24,671
<b>What is your definition of intelligence?</b>

12253
06:14:24,671 --> 06:14:27,374
<b>mm-hmm, so as I was just saying</b>

12254
06:14:27,374 --> 06:14:28,842
<b>Rich Sutton talked about this</b>

12255
06:14:28,842 --> 06:14:31,045
<b>he feels that squirrel intelligence is the real intelligence</b>

12256
06:14:31,478 --> 06:14:34,248
<b>I think his framing is a bit different</b>

12257
06:14:34,782 --> 06:14:37,084
<b>he's not positioning from a human perspective</b>

12258
06:14:37,117 --> 06:14:39,186
<b>looking at things from an anthropocentric view</b>

12259
06:14:39,586 --> 06:14:40,521
<b>he's standing at the universe</b>

12260
06:14:40,521 --> 06:14:42,322
<b>and the creator's perspective</b>

12261
06:14:43,057 --> 06:14:44,224
<b>from this angle</b>

12262
06:14:44,391 --> 06:14:45,459
<b>of course</b>

12263
06:14:45,626 --> 06:14:48,862
<b>being able to recreate a squirrel</b>

12264
06:14:48,862 --> 06:14:49,630
<b>is greater than your</b>

12265
06:14:49,630 --> 06:14:53,901
<b>human civilization in these 530 million years</b>

12266
06:14:53,901 --> 06:14:56,170
<b>the things created in the last 8 seconds</b>

12267
06:14:56,470 --> 06:14:58,005
<b>by far</b>

12268
06:14:58,005 --> 06:14:58,639
<b>in this sense</b>

12269
06:14:58,639 --> 06:14:59,440
<b>I think</b>

12270
06:14:59,440 --> 06:15:00,307
<b>that's elevated the discussion</b>

12271
06:15:00,307 --> 06:15:02,676
<b>I think that elevated perspective has merit</b>

12272
06:15:02,676 --> 06:15:04,178
<b>but defining intelligence</b>

12273
06:15:04,178 --> 06:15:07,214
<b>I don't want to give it a definition</b>

12274
06:15:07,214 --> 06:15:09,783
<b>I think different animals have different intelligence</b>

12275
06:15:09,783 --> 06:15:12,019
<b>and humans have human-level intelligence</b>

12276
06:15:12,019 --> 06:15:13,020
<b>Mm-hmm</b>

12277
06:15:13,086 --> 06:15:16,023
<b>and what I want to encourage everyone to do</b>

12278
06:15:16,390 --> 06:15:18,025
<b>don't only focus on what</b>

12279
06:15:18,025 --> 06:15:19,893
<b>we as individuals cannot do</b>

12280
06:15:20,227 --> 06:15:22,496
<b>pay attention to what we're already doing well</b>

12281
06:15:22,830 --> 06:15:25,199
<b>pay attention to what a 4-year-old child</b>

12282
06:15:25,199 --> 06:15:27,868
<b>or a child of a few years old does very well</b>

12283
06:15:28,202 --> 06:15:29,436
<b>those things</b>

12284
06:15:29,436 --> 06:15:32,072
<b>are actually what our world model</b>

12285
06:15:32,306 --> 06:15:34,007
<b>next needs to focus on solving</b>

12286
06:15:34,241 --> 06:15:35,509
<b>mm-hmm, so this is also</b>

12287
06:15:35,509 --> 06:15:37,444
<b>why Robotics is ultimately</b>

12288
06:15:37,444 --> 06:15:38,846
<b>a very fitting outlet</b>

12289
06:15:39,113 --> 06:15:41,982
<b>because before you talk about AGI</b>

12290
06:15:41,982 --> 06:15:43,984
<b>or super intelligence</b>

12291
06:15:44,418 --> 06:15:47,254
<b>can we first have a sufficiently reliable</b>

12292
06:15:47,387 --> 06:15:48,822
<b>and general robot</b>

12293
06:15:49,189 --> 06:15:51,024
<b>that can function in our home environment</b>

12294
06:15:51,024 --> 06:15:52,860
<b>and help with household chores</b>

12295
06:15:52,860 --> 06:15:55,062
<b>right, because a few-year-old child</b>

12296
06:15:55,062 --> 06:15:57,231
<b>can actually do many, many household chores</b>

12297
06:15:57,231 --> 06:15:58,999
<b>there's actually a list</b>

12298
06:15:58,999 --> 06:16:00,267
<b>you can search for it online</b>

12299
06:16:00,467 --> 06:16:02,236
<b>a 12-year-old child</b>

12300
06:16:02,236 --> 06:16:03,904
<b>can basically do all the household chores</b>

12301
06:16:04,638 --> 06:16:07,674
<b>but is there a robot right now</b>

12302
06:16:07,808 --> 06:16:10,310
<b>that can function like a 12-year-old child</b>

12303
06:16:10,577 --> 06:16:12,079
<b>and handle these chores?</b>

12304
06:16:12,079 --> 06:16:12,880
<b>of course not</b>

12305
06:16:13,180 --> 06:16:14,281
<b>Jie Tan from DeepMind</b>

12306
06:16:14,281 --> 06:16:14,781
<b>Jie Tan</b>

12307
06:16:14,781 --> 06:16:18,085
<b>he also says that robotic development is extremely uneven</b>

12308
06:16:18,085 --> 06:16:18,986
<b>extremely imbalanced</b>

12309
06:16:18,986 --> 06:16:20,988
<b>its developmental trajectory compared to a child's</b>

12310
06:16:20,988 --> 06:16:22,022
<b>is different</b>

12311
06:16:22,022 --> 06:16:23,223
<b>mm-hmm, for example</b>

12312
06:16:23,223 --> 06:16:26,994
<b>the physical capabilities of robots' limbs have now surpassed</b>

12313
06:16:26,994 --> 06:16:29,296
<b>they've already surpassed humans</b>

12314
06:16:29,296 --> 06:16:29,730
<b>Mm-hmm</b>

12315
06:16:29,730 --> 06:16:32,399
<b>but many other capabilities are still not as good as a child's</b>

12316
06:16:32,633 --> 06:16:33,100
<b>because of the brain</b>

12317
06:16:33,100 --> 06:16:34,635
<b>nobody is building the brain</b>

12318
06:16:34,668 --> 06:16:36,703
<b>nobody is building a robot brain</b>

12319
06:16:36,703 --> 06:16:39,239
<b>all the robotics startups</b>

12320
06:16:39,273 --> 06:16:41,408
<b>including the robotics divisions at big companies</b>

12321
06:16:41,441 --> 06:16:43,043
<b>haven't solved this</b>

12322
06:16:43,210 --> 06:16:44,511
<b>Doesn't DeepMind count?</b>

12323
06:16:44,845 --> 06:16:46,647
<b>DeepMind is now entirely based on Gemini</b>

12324
06:16:46,847 --> 06:16:49,216
<b>so it's also working within the VLA framework</b>

12325
06:16:49,216 --> 06:16:50,050
<b>Yes</b>

12326
06:16:50,050 --> 06:16:51,251
<b>everything converges to</b>

12327
06:16:51,251 --> 06:16:53,787
<b>Gemini</b>

12328
06:16:53,787 --> 06:16:54,254
<b>Oh</b>

12329
06:16:54,254 --> 06:16:57,391
<b>but this needs a second half of pre-training</b>

12330
06:16:57,391 --> 06:16:57,991
<b>Mm-hmm</b>

12331
06:16:57,991 --> 06:17:00,494
<b>in Shunyu Yao's classic formulation</b>

12332
06:17:00,494 --> 06:17:03,230
<b>[laughter] I think there needs to be a second half</b>

12333
06:17:03,230 --> 06:17:05,065
<b>but I think this is the second half of pre-training</b>

12334
06:17:05,065 --> 06:17:05,599
<b>Mm-hmm</b>

12335
06:17:05,599 --> 06:17:07,668
<b>Jim Fan recently also expressed the same view</b>

12336
06:17:08,368 --> 06:17:10,404
<b>so this pre-training is the world model</b>

12337
06:17:10,404 --> 06:17:12,806
<b>who will do this pre-training?</b>

12338
06:17:13,373 --> 06:17:15,242
<b>that's not clear to me</b>

12339
06:17:15,409 --> 06:17:15,876
<b>if I knew</b>

12340
06:17:15,876 --> 06:17:17,878
<b>there was another place that could also do this</b>

12341
06:17:17,878 --> 06:17:19,379
<b>then I might actually reconsider</b>

12342
06:17:19,379 --> 06:17:21,448
<b>I wouldn't necessarily need to be</b>
<b>at this startup</b>

12343
06:17:21,448 --> 06:17:22,382
<b>doing this myself</b>

12344
06:17:22,516 --> 06:17:23,317
<b>right?</b>

12345
06:17:24,051 --> 06:17:25,118
<b>robotics startups</b>

12346
06:17:25,118 --> 06:17:28,121
<b>have no energy to do this</b>

12347
06:17:28,121 --> 06:17:30,824
<b>they need to put their resources</b>

12348
06:17:30,824 --> 06:17:32,626
<b>into the so-called hardware</b>

12349
06:17:32,626 --> 06:17:33,927
<b>scaling law</b>

12350
06:17:34,227 --> 06:17:34,861
<b>that is</b>

12351
06:17:34,861 --> 06:17:36,263
<b>you need to buy more robots</b>

12352
06:17:36,263 --> 06:17:37,464
<b>to deploy these robots</b>

12353
06:17:37,464 --> 06:17:40,267
<b>or do these things in simulators</b>

12354
06:17:40,267 --> 06:17:42,402
<b>these imitation learning approaches</b>

12355
06:17:42,469 --> 06:17:44,304
<b>that can give you a good enough</b>

12356
06:17:44,304 --> 06:17:47,808
<b>to solve some specific problems</b>

12357
06:17:47,808 --> 06:17:49,576
<b>in the short term</b>

12358
06:17:49,576 --> 06:17:51,645
<b>a robotics team that creates value</b>

12359
06:17:52,045 --> 06:17:53,013
<b>What about PI (Physical Intelligence)?</b>

12360
06:17:53,480 --> 06:17:55,215
<b>VLA, right?</b>

12361
06:17:55,215 --> 06:17:56,049
<b>PI is the same</b>

12362
06:17:56,049 --> 06:17:58,218
<b>PI is already very, very research-oriented</b>

12363
06:17:58,485 --> 06:18:00,387
<b>and doing very, very well</b>

12364
06:18:00,387 --> 06:18:01,021
<b>and is inspiring</b>

12365
06:18:01,021 --> 06:18:02,055
<b>as a company</b>

12366
06:18:02,389 --> 06:18:05,092
<b>but again, they won't do pre-training</b>

12367
06:18:05,092 --> 06:18:06,260
<b>they won't do pre-training</b>

12368
06:18:07,127 --> 06:18:08,095
<b>they'll take</b>

12369
06:18:08,095 --> 06:18:11,531
<b>language models as their foundation</b>

12370
06:18:11,598 --> 06:18:12,065
<b>Yeah</b>

12371
06:18:12,065 --> 06:18:12,799
<b>right?</b>

12372
06:18:12,799 --> 06:18:15,435
<b>How should we understand your second half of pre-training?</b>

12373
06:18:15,669 --> 06:18:16,770
<b>what goes in</b>

12374
06:18:16,770 --> 06:18:17,571
<b>what comes out</b>

12375
06:18:17,804 --> 06:18:18,205
<b>I don't know</b>

12376
06:18:18,205 --> 06:18:19,239
<b>at least the first step is</b>

12377
06:18:19,306 --> 06:18:20,007
<b>in the long run</b>

12378
06:18:20,007 --> 06:18:21,108
<b>the inputs are all</b>

12379
06:18:21,108 --> 06:18:22,876
<b>continuous-space signals as I just described</b>

12380
06:18:23,076 --> 06:18:24,378
<b>high-dimensional</b>

12381
06:18:24,478 --> 06:18:25,612
<b>potentially noisy signals</b>

12382
06:18:25,612 --> 06:18:26,246
<b>Mm-hmm</b>

12383
06:18:26,246 --> 06:18:28,215
<b>at first it might still be video</b>

12384
06:18:28,215 --> 06:18:30,817
<b>but we might also have multi-modal encoders</b>

12385
06:18:30,884 --> 06:18:32,919
<b>to handle different</b>

12386
06:18:32,919 --> 06:18:34,655
<b>signals beyond visual</b>

12387
06:18:35,522 --> 06:18:37,291
<b>and the outputs</b>

12388
06:18:37,291 --> 06:18:38,992
<b>that's a research question</b>

12389
06:18:39,259 --> 06:18:41,628
<b>the self-supervised question is still unknown</b>

12390
06:18:41,628 --> 06:18:42,329
<b>I</b>

12391
06:18:42,329 --> 06:18:44,264
<b>not necessarily unknown</b>

12392
06:18:44,264 --> 06:18:45,899
<b>but</b>

12393
06:18:45,899 --> 06:18:47,567
<b>it may become clearer later</b>

12394
06:18:47,834 --> 06:18:48,635
<b>Mm-hmm</b>

12395
06:18:49,369 --> 06:18:50,771
<b>but</b>

12396
06:18:50,771 --> 06:18:52,472
<b>I think</b>

12397
06:18:52,506 --> 06:18:53,774
<b>it's definitely not that simple</b>

12398
06:18:53,774 --> 06:18:56,643
<b>but I think that's where the excitement lies</b>

12399
06:18:58,812 --> 06:19:00,013
<b>I also find it quite interesting</b>

12400
06:19:00,013 --> 06:19:01,248
<b>because the first time we met</b>

12401
06:19:01,248 --> 06:19:03,617
<b>you said "you are not the chosen one"</b>

12402
06:19:03,617 --> 06:19:04,918
<b>"you are just the normal one"</b>

12403
06:19:04,918 --> 06:19:08,188
<b>why do you like saying this?</b>

12404
06:19:08,188 --> 06:19:10,524
<b>No</b>
<b>you see, throughout our conversation we discussed my</b>

12405
06:19:10,524 --> 06:19:12,459
<b>growth story</b>

12406
06:19:12,459 --> 06:19:14,594
<b>I</b>
<b>I didn't expect we'd talk about all this</b>

12407
06:19:14,594 --> 06:19:17,331
<b>but</b>

12408
06:19:17,331 --> 06:19:19,399
<b>I definitely don't feel like a chosen one</b>

12409
06:19:19,399 --> 06:19:23,070
<b>[laughter]</b>
<b>this quote is actually from a team I love</b>

12410
06:19:23,070 --> 06:19:24,404
<b>Liverpool, right?</b>

12411
06:19:24,404 --> 06:19:25,572
<b>I'm a KOP (the famous terrace at Anfield and symbol of devoted Liverpool fans)</b>

12412
06:19:25,672 --> 06:19:28,041
<b>for over 20 years</b>

12413
06:19:28,041 --> 06:19:29,209
<b>[laughter]</b>

12414
06:19:29,209 --> 06:19:31,845
<b>I think there's a bit of compatible spirit</b>

12415
06:19:31,845 --> 06:19:34,114
<b>and my favorite manager</b>

12416
06:19:34,114 --> 06:19:35,048
<b>Klopp</b>

12417
06:19:35,215 --> 06:19:36,183
<b>Jürgen Klopp</b>

12418
06:19:36,450 --> 06:19:37,284
<b>[laughter]</b>

12419
06:19:37,284 --> 06:19:40,120
<b>he was half-joking when he said to everyone</b>

12420
06:19:40,187 --> 06:19:41,121
<b>when another manager</b>

12421
06:19:41,121 --> 06:19:41,621
<b>José Mourinho</b>

12422
06:19:41,621 --> 06:19:43,690
<b>said "I am the special one"</b>

12423
06:19:43,690 --> 06:19:44,925
<b>I'm the special one</b>

12424
06:19:45,492 --> 06:19:47,994
<b>then Klopp said</b>

12425
06:19:47,994 --> 06:19:49,129
<b>"I'm not the special one"</b>

12426
06:19:49,129 --> 06:19:50,864
<b>"I'm the normal one"</b>

12427
06:19:51,064 --> 06:19:54,501
<b>and I think</b>

12428
06:19:54,501 --> 06:19:56,036
<b>on one hand he himself is very punk</b>

12429
06:19:56,036 --> 06:19:57,571
<b>he has that rock 'n' roll spirit</b>

12430
06:19:57,571 --> 06:19:58,772
<b>[laughter]</b>

12431
06:19:58,772 --> 06:20:00,107
<b>Uh</b>

12432
06:20:00,107 --> 06:20:02,376
<b>and he often tells everyone</b>

12433
06:20:02,376 --> 06:20:04,411
<b>that his role in the team</b>

12434
06:20:04,578 --> 06:20:06,213
<b>is like a battery</b>

12435
06:20:06,480 --> 06:20:08,415
<b>he hopes through his own passion</b>

12436
06:20:08,415 --> 06:20:11,318
<b>and his own energy, you know</b>

12437
06:20:11,318 --> 06:20:13,053
<b>to let others</b>

12438
06:20:13,053 --> 06:20:14,121
<b>generate electricity for others</b>

12439
06:20:14,121 --> 06:20:14,988
<b>empower</b>

12440
06:20:14,988 --> 06:20:16,189
<b>empower others</b>

12441
06:20:16,189 --> 06:20:17,057
<b>mm-hmm, right</b>

12442
06:20:17,057 --> 06:20:18,058
<b>I also want to be that kind of person</b>

12443
06:20:18,058 --> 06:20:20,260
<b>I also want to be for a team</b>

12444
06:20:20,260 --> 06:20:22,729
<b>whether that team is in academia</b>

12445
06:20:22,729 --> 06:20:25,565
<b>or in a startup, a battery</b>

12446
06:20:25,565 --> 06:20:27,234
<b>I think this is actually not easy</b>

12447
06:20:27,234 --> 06:20:28,301
<b>because sometimes</b>

12448
06:20:29,069 --> 06:20:30,971
<b>everyone has their moments of discouragement</b>

12449
06:20:30,971 --> 06:20:31,471
<b>Mm-hmm</b>

12450
06:20:31,471 --> 06:20:33,273
<b>I also want to</b>

12451
06:20:33,707 --> 06:20:34,875
<b>so</b>

12452
06:20:34,875 --> 06:20:35,776
<b>complain more</b>

12453
06:20:35,776 --> 06:20:37,611
<b>and let out my feelings</b>

12454
06:20:37,611 --> 06:20:39,179
<b>but I'm gradually coming to feel</b>

12455
06:20:39,413 --> 06:20:41,815
<b>in academia, like in front of students</b>

12456
06:20:41,815 --> 06:20:44,885
<b>and in front of the startup team</b>

12457
06:20:45,085 --> 06:20:48,622
<b>someone needs to play that battery role</b>

12458
06:20:48,622 --> 06:20:51,525
<b>or I think Yann is a giant battery</b>

12459
06:20:51,525 --> 06:20:52,526
<b>he inspired me</b>

12460
06:20:52,526 --> 06:20:54,861
<b>but I hope to pass this electrical charge through me</b>

12461
06:20:54,861 --> 06:20:55,896
<b>and send it further</b>

12462
06:20:57,531 --> 06:21:01,768
<b>What was the last time you felt discouraged, and why?</b>

12463
06:21:02,602 --> 06:21:04,004
<b>I feel discouraged every day</b>

12464
06:21:04,004 --> 06:21:06,106
<b>I think it's become</b>

12465
06:21:06,106 --> 06:21:07,841
<b>a kind of researcher's fate</b>

12466
06:21:07,841 --> 06:21:11,812
<b>I think everyone has this underlying melancholy</b>

12467
06:21:12,112 --> 06:21:14,414
<b>because the process of research inquiry</b>

12468
06:21:14,414 --> 06:21:18,885
<b>is like groping around in a dark</b>

12469
06:21:18,885 --> 06:21:21,221
