13035
06:39:39,985 --> 06:39:41,654
<b>I don't think it's necessarily that simple</b>

13036
06:39:41,921 --> 06:39:44,490
<b>Our studio is called Language and World Studio</b>

13037
06:39:44,490 --> 06:39:45,925
<b>what comes to mind when you hear that name?</b>

13038
06:39:45,925 --> 06:39:47,993
<b>what are you thinking?</b>

13039
06:39:47,993 --> 06:39:50,329
<b>I see you wrote me a line: let go of</b>

13040
06:39:50,329 --> 06:39:51,430
<b>uh, called</b>

13041
06:39:51,830 --> 06:39:53,098
<b>let go of Wittgenstein</b>

13042
06:39:53,098 --> 06:39:54,300
<b>let go of Wittgenstein</b>

13043
06:39:54,300 --> 06:39:55,834
<b>well, that's not a great way to end</b>

13044
06:39:55,834 --> 06:39:56,802
<b>I'm going to start complaining again</b>

13045
06:39:56,802 --> 06:39:58,270
<b>right, go ahead</b>
<b>you complain — I say, let go of Wittgenstein</b>

13046
06:39:58,270 --> 06:39:59,104
<b>means you shouldn't</b>

13047
06:39:59,104 --> 06:40:00,673
<b>people shouldn't take Wittgenstein</b>

13048
06:40:00,673 --> 06:40:01,674
<b>and really stretch him</b>

13049
06:40:01,674 --> 06:40:05,110
<b>using it as a language boundary</b>

13050
06:40:05,110 --> 06:40:06,312
<b>meaning the limits of my world</b>

13051
06:40:06,312 --> 06:40:08,581
<b>and use that quote as endorsement for LLMs</b>

13052
06:40:08,581 --> 06:40:10,316
<b>or linguistic determinism</b>

13053
06:40:10,316 --> 06:40:12,851
<b>so that's completely absurd</b>

13054
06:40:12,851 --> 06:40:13,585
<b>and likewise</b>

13055
06:40:13,585 --> 06:40:14,787
<b>there are other quotes</b>

13056
06:40:14,787 --> 06:40:16,088
<b>like people citing Feynman</b>

13057
06:40:16,088 --> 06:40:18,424
<b>Feynman said what I cannot create</b>

13058
06:40:18,424 --> 06:40:19,892
<b>I do not understand</b>

13059
06:40:19,892 --> 06:40:20,426
<b>this</b>

13060
06:40:20,426 --> 06:40:22,661
<b>being used to endorse unified models</b>

13061
06:40:22,695 --> 06:40:23,429
<b>I think</b>

13062
06:40:23,429 --> 06:40:25,664
<b>both of these things are really unacceptable to me</b>

13063
06:40:26,098 --> 06:40:27,700
<b>what's the first thing?</b>

13064
06:40:27,700 --> 06:40:29,468
<b>the first is Wittgenstein, right?</b>

13065
06:40:29,601 --> 06:40:31,904
<b>when he spoke of the limits of language</b>

13066
06:40:31,904 --> 06:40:33,272
<b>as the limits of my world</b>

13067
06:40:33,305 --> 06:40:34,840
<b>there were strong preconditions</b>

13068
06:40:34,840 --> 06:40:36,709
<b>in his Tractatus Logico-Philosophicus</b>

13069
06:40:36,709 --> 06:40:39,612
<b>what he discussed in the Tractatus</b>

13070
06:40:39,612 --> 06:40:42,214
<b>was that</b>

13071
06:40:42,214 --> 06:40:43,582
<b>your</b>

13072
06:40:43,582 --> 06:40:48,387
<b>the language he referred to targets what can be captured in propositions</b>

13073
06:40:48,387 --> 06:40:50,589
<b>the limits of the world that can be described</b>

13074
06:40:50,622 --> 06:40:53,292
<b>and this does not represent the general</b>

13075
06:40:53,292 --> 06:40:55,928
<b>the entirety of what we call the world</b>

13076
06:40:56,095 --> 06:40:56,495
<b>[laughter]</b>

13077
06:40:56,495 --> 06:40:58,631
<b>so</b>

13078
06:40:58,631 --> 06:41:00,432
<b>first, the language he spoke of</b>

13079
06:41:00,432 --> 06:41:02,067
<b>and the world he spoke of</b>

13080
06:41:02,067 --> 06:41:04,436
<b>are already different from the language in today's LLMs</b>

13081
06:41:04,436 --> 06:41:05,504
<b>and the world it refers to</b>

13082
06:41:05,637 --> 06:41:08,007
<b>second, in his later period Wittgenstein</b>

13083
06:41:08,007 --> 06:41:10,776
<b>had completely overturned his earlier</b>

13084
06:41:10,776 --> 06:41:13,412
<b>entire philosophical system</b>

13085
06:41:14,113 --> 06:41:15,714
<b>he later stopped saying that</b>

13086
06:41:16,215 --> 06:41:18,417
<b>and what he talked about instead was</b>

13087
06:41:18,417 --> 06:41:19,985
<b>language is actually a game</b>

13088
06:41:19,985 --> 06:41:22,488
<b>the so-called concept of language games</b>

13089
06:41:22,521 --> 06:41:25,057
<b>meaning language itself has no inherent meaning</b>

13090
06:41:25,057 --> 06:41:27,259
<b>these symbols themselves have no meaning</b>

13091
06:41:28,260 --> 06:41:29,695
<b>the reason they acquire meaning</b>

13092
06:41:29,695 --> 06:41:33,399
<b>is because they are connected to real-world practice</b>

13093
06:41:33,432 --> 06:41:34,466
<b>and engaged with it</b>

13094
06:41:34,466 --> 06:41:35,267
<b>Mm-hmm</b>

13095
06:41:35,300 --> 06:41:37,503
<b>and this is very much the world model view</b>

13096
06:41:37,670 --> 06:41:39,004
<b>that is</b>

13097
06:41:39,004 --> 06:41:39,905
<b>we're not saying</b>

13098
06:41:39,905 --> 06:41:42,608
<b>that language can perfectly</b>

13099
06:41:42,608 --> 06:41:44,710
<b>represent the entire world</b>

13100
06:41:44,977 --> 06:41:48,814
<b>what we're saying is that the world's practice</b>

13101
06:41:48,814 --> 06:41:53,652
<b>the world's actions determine the game of language</b>

13102
06:41:53,686 --> 06:41:55,087
<b>its intension and extension</b>

13103
06:41:55,587 --> 06:41:57,856
<b>mm-hmm, again</b>

13104
06:41:57,856 --> 06:41:58,924
<b>I don't understand philosophy</b>

13105
06:41:58,924 --> 06:42:00,125
<b>I don't understand Wittgenstein either</b>

13106
06:42:00,325 --> 06:42:02,995
<b>but I just don't like seeing in people's papers</b>

13107
06:42:03,128 --> 06:42:05,864
<b>opening with a pulled quote</b>

13108
06:42:05,864 --> 06:42:08,667
<b>I think that doesn't fit my aesthetic sensibilities</b>

13109
06:42:08,834 --> 06:42:12,071
<b>the Feynman quote is the same</b>

13110
06:42:12,071 --> 06:42:13,305
<b>mm-hmm, he said</b>

13111
06:42:13,305 --> 06:42:14,606
<b>what I cannot create</b>

13112
06:42:14,606 --> 06:42:16,208
<b>I do not understand</b>

13113
06:42:16,208 --> 06:42:17,609
<b>that quote itself is not wrong</b>

13114
06:42:17,876 --> 06:42:22,081
<b>but the create and understand he's referring to mean</b>

13115
06:42:22,081 --> 06:42:23,415
<b>for example, we have a world</b>

13116
06:42:23,415 --> 06:42:25,984
<b>we want to understand this world</b>

13117
06:42:25,984 --> 06:42:27,052
<b>we want to transform this world</b>

13118
06:42:27,052 --> 06:42:28,587
<b>we want to understand the world</b>

13119
06:42:28,587 --> 06:42:29,621
<b>through transforming it</b>

13120
06:42:29,722 --> 06:42:30,723
<b>whatever</b>

13121
06:42:30,723 --> 06:42:31,857
<b>the things he was talking about</b>

13122
06:42:31,857 --> 06:42:34,426
<b>are still within a real, concrete world</b>

13123
06:42:34,493 --> 06:42:35,828
<b>requiring some kind of action</b>

13124
06:42:35,928 --> 06:42:37,696
<b>mm-hmm, even when you're in class</b>

13125
06:42:37,696 --> 06:42:39,832
<b>you go and make a PowerPoint</b>

13126
06:42:39,965 --> 06:42:41,800
<b>you're still engaged in a process of creation</b>

13127
06:42:42,067 --> 06:42:43,669
<b>but now many people take this quote</b>

13128
06:42:43,669 --> 06:42:46,572
<b>and use it to make this kind of, uh</b>

13129
06:42:46,572 --> 06:42:50,175
<b>endorsement for some simple unified system</b>

13130
06:42:50,175 --> 06:42:52,578
<b>that's logically untenable too</b>

13131
06:42:53,412 --> 06:42:56,415
<b>we can't simply reduce creation</b>

13132
06:42:56,515 --> 06:42:59,184
<b>to a diffusion model</b>

13133
06:42:59,518 --> 06:43:02,020
<b>its backpropagation loss</b>

13134
06:43:02,020 --> 06:43:03,922
<b>that's completely absurd</b>

13135
06:43:03,922 --> 06:43:04,723
<b>mm-hmm, right?</b>

13136
06:43:04,857 --> 06:43:07,593
<b>so</b>

13137
06:43:07,593 --> 06:43:08,594
<b>I don't know</b>

13138
06:43:08,594 --> 06:43:10,062
<b>I think</b>

13139
06:43:10,295 --> 06:43:12,131
<b>maybe it's like when I was a kid</b>

13140
06:43:12,131 --> 06:43:15,200
<b>overusing famous quotes in essays</b>

13141
06:43:15,200 --> 06:43:18,437
<b>now seeing these things gives me a bit of PTSD</b>

13142
06:43:18,570 --> 06:43:22,040
<b>and I think as Kaiming said</b>

13143
06:43:22,040 --> 06:43:23,809
<b>everyone should read more philosophy</b>

13144
06:43:23,976 --> 06:43:25,511
<b>I think that's quite worthwhile</b>

13145
06:43:25,511 --> 06:43:28,614
<b>mm-hmm, at the very start you said you believe in fate</b>

13146
06:43:28,614 --> 06:43:29,648
<b>and believe in it more and more</b>

13147
06:43:29,648 --> 06:43:31,650
<b>where do you feel fate is pushing you now?</b>

13148
06:43:32,718 --> 06:43:33,786
<b>Ah</b>

13149
06:43:34,987 --> 06:43:38,457
<b>I don't know</b>

13150
06:43:38,791 --> 06:43:40,492
<b>is fate pushing me?</b>

13151
06:43:40,492 --> 06:43:43,262
<b>it doesn't seem like it</b>

13152
06:43:43,262 --> 06:43:43,662
<b>I think</b>

13153
06:43:43,662 --> 06:43:46,665
<b>there's no feeling of being pushed by fate</b>

13154
06:43:46,665 --> 06:43:47,966
<b>mm-hmm, just</b>

13155
06:43:49,434 --> 06:43:54,039
<b>mm-hmm, when the next time I need to make a choice comes</b>

13156
06:43:54,039 --> 06:43:55,574
<b>I just hope for good fortune</b>

13157
06:43:55,808 --> 06:43:58,010
<b>Is this world a giant world model?</b>

13158
06:43:58,310 --> 06:44:00,078
<b>of course the world is a giant world model</b>

13159
06:44:00,279 --> 06:44:02,047
<b>can you predict fate then?</b>

13160
06:44:02,581 --> 06:44:04,483
<b>uh, I don't think so</b>

13161
06:44:04,883 --> 06:44:05,717
<b>why not?</b>

13162
06:44:06,185 --> 06:44:06,685
<b>Mm-hmm</b>

13163
06:44:06,685 --> 06:44:08,287
<b>because we don't have enough resources</b>

13164
06:44:09,254 --> 06:44:09,588
<b>Oh</b>

13165
06:44:09,588 --> 06:44:12,991
<b>you'd need a computer as large as the Earth</b>

